{"parentUuid":"9aa24d77-89fa-486b-9866-2b2defa521f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_901d4d9f31c5491e8507fa61","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to configure FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader) for the nucleo-n657x0-q development board to make external flash work with power-off saving. They want me to reference the mboot configuration from /home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython. Let me analyze what's needed step by step.\n\nFirst, I need to understand what FSBL is in the context of STM32 - it's the First Stage Boot Loader that initializes the system, including external memory interfaces like FMC (Flexible Memory Controller) or XSPI (for newer STM32 chips like STM32N6 series).\n\n\nThe STM32N657X0 on the nucleo-n657x0-q board uses XSPI (Extended Serial Peripheral Interface) for external flash, so I'll need to examine the reference mboot configuration to see how it's set up for that specific memory interface.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":22214,"output_tokens":0}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"e08e909f-546d-40a5-a171-d8d42ab12f49","timestamp":"2026-08-21T01:54:43.359Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
