rchitecture Support\n\n**Architecture source:** `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/`\n\nKey files:\n- `Kconfig` -- chip selection for `ARCH_CHIP_STM32N657X0`, selects `STM32_STM32N6XXXX`, enables `STM32_HAVE_USART1`\n- `stm32n6xx_rcc.c` -- PLL1 clock configuration, enables all AXISRAM bank clocks, enables GPIO ports A-H/N-Q and PWR on AHB4, USART1 on APB2. Contains XSPI2 kernel clock reference via IC3.\n- `stm32_start.c`, `stm32_idle.c`, `stm32_irq.c`, `stm32_gpio.c`, `stm32_serial.c`, `stm32_lowputc.c`, `stm32_pwr.c`, `stm32_timerisr.c`\n- `hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h` -- full peripheral base address map\n- `hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h`, `stm32n6xxx_pwr.h`, `stm32n6xxx_gpio.h`, `stm32n6xxx_uart.h`, `stm32n6xxx_syscfg.h`, `stm32n6xxx_pinmap.h`\n\n**Architecture includes:** `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/include/stm32n6/`\n\n- `chip.h` -- SRAM size (4 MiB), 12 GPIO ports, 1 USART; comment: \"STM32N6 has no internal flash. Code runs from on-chip AXI SRAM (loaded by debugger in DEV mode, or by an FSBL from external XSPI flash in normal boot)\"\n- `irq.h`, `stm32n6xx_irq.h` -- 195 external IRQs including XSPI1/2/3\n\n**Documentation:** `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/Documentation/platforms/arm/stm32n6/`\n\n- `index.rst` -- platform overview: Cortex-M55, only STM32N657X0 supported, XSPI listed as \"No\" in peripheral support table\n- `boards/nucleo-n657x0-q/index.rst` -- full board doc with features, pin mapping, build/flash instructions. States: \"External XSPI NOR flash interface\" is a board feature but \"XSPI flash boot\" is \"not yet wired up\"\n\n---\n\n## 3. XSPI (Extended SPI) References\n\nXSPI is referenced **only as infrastructure definitions** -- no driver implementation exists.\n\n**Memory map** (`/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h`):\n```c\n#define STM32_XSPI1_BANK      0x90000000    /* XSPI1 memory-mapped region */\n#define STM32_XSPI2_BANK      0x70000000    /* XSPI2 memory-mapped region 