{"parentUuid":"3e3a0c8b-f570-4de9-8259-4324df8f875f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_7c33dc575dd943acb2cc91eb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me synthesize all this into a comprehensive step-by-step guide for the user.\n\nKey facts:\n1. **Nucleo-N657X0-Q** board has **MX25UM51245G** (512Mbit = 64MB) external flash on XSPI2\n2. The existing NuttX port runs only from SRAM (DEV mode via debugger), no XSPI support\n3. The MicroPython project has a complete working FSBL/mboot with XSPI driver for the same board\n4. STM32N6 has NO internal flash - code must run from external XSPI flash (XIP) or SRAM\n\n\n5. The boot sequence flows from the hardware ROM loading the FSBL into SRAM, which then initializes XSPI and memory-maps the flash, allowing the main application to execute directly from flash at 0x70080000\n\nTo implement this in NuttX, I need to create an XSPI driver, build an FSBL that initializes the flash, set up linker scripts for XIP execution, add board-level configuration, and modify the build system to support this boot chain.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":2853,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53760}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"472d5c66-bc5e-4e71-ae01-bdcc9a3c5743","timestamp":"2026-08-21T01:59:47.642Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
