m32n6-nucleo-n657x0-q-nsh/` -- Full build output directory (50+ MB of generated CMake/cache files)\n\nThese contain hundreds of auto-generated references to `nucleo-n657x0-q` in CMake cache files, `cmake_install.cmake`, etc. These are build artifacts, not source files.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Git Rerere Cache (.repo)\n\n**File:** `/home/warner/openvela/.repo/project-objects/nuttx.git/rr-cache/e71cea72de3cac425fa530275b935be79a36b512/preimage`\n\nContains a merge-conflict preimage with the board's Kconfig registration entries (lines 3620-3621, 4429, 5578-5579), indicating this board was added as part of a branch that was merged/rebased.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Claude Settings\n\n**File:** `/home/warner/openvela/.claude/settings.local.json`\n\nLine 16: Contains a previously-approved bash command: `./tools/configure.sh nucleo-n657x0-q:nsh`\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe nucleo-n657x0-q board exists in **three main locations**:\n\n1. **NuttX BSP** (`nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/`) -- 15 source files, the primary board support package with 3 defconfig variants (nsh, leds, ostest)\n2. **MicroPython port** (`atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/NUCLEO_N657X0/`) -- 43 files including camera/TFT drivers\n3. **TinyUSB BSP** (`atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/tinyusb/hw/bsp/stm32n6/boards/stm32n657nucleo/`) -- minimal board header\n\nPlus documentation in `nuttx/Documentation/` and `docs/stm32n657-development-guide.md`, and build artifacts in `cmake_out/` and `out/`. No references were found in the `vendor/`, `apps/`, `frameworks/`, `external/`, `packages/`, `tests/`, or `build/` directories.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>42646</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>57</tool_uses><duration_ms>294264</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-21T01:59:59.670Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb39ce4a-6e98-4ee2-8e8d-0fb4dc59e40a","timestamp":"2026-08-21T01:59:59.670Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/op