{"parentUuid":"bd4011b5-9960-4354-bdaa-53f4901255a7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad5bad901e85ebf5b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_e7f9c3d0ae724f538c5e61a7</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-warner-openvela/6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323/tasks/ad5bad901e85ebf5b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Read hardware porting guide\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Now I have all the information needed. Here is the comprehensive summary.\n\n---\n\n## Comprehensive Summary: New Hardware Adaptation (新硬件适配) Contest Track\n\n### 1. Directory Structure for a Contest Board\n\nBased on the contest manifest (`/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui.xml`), the actual contest board template (`/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/`), and the porting guide (`/home/warner/openvela/docs/zh-cn/chip_porting/porting_guide.md`), a contest board must follow this structure:\n\n**Team repository layout** (inside `contest2026_&lt;number&gt;_&lt;teamname&gt;/`):\n```\ncontest2026_&lt;number&gt;_&lt;teamname&gt;/\n  board/\n    contest_board/          # &lt;-- This gets symlinked to vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_&lt;number&gt;_board\n      Kconfig\n      CMakeLists.txt\n      README.md\n      configs/\n        nsh/\n          defconfig\n      include/\n        board.h\n      scripts/\n        ld.script           # Linker script\n        Make.defs           # Build configuration\n      src/\n        CMakeLists.txt\n        board_boot.c        # Board initialization (openvela_board_initialize)\n        &lt;vendor&gt;_bringup.c  # Peripheral bringup\n        &lt;vendor&gt;_appinit.c  # App initialization\n        etc/\n          init.d/\n            rcS             # Startup script\n            rc.sysinit       # Core app startup\n          group\n          passwd\n  logs/                     # AI Coding logs\n  README.md                 # Project description\n```\n\n**Full vendor directory structure** (as documented in `/home/warner/openvela/docs/zh-cn/chip_porting/Vendor.md`):\n```\nvendor/&lt;vendor_name&gt;/\n  boards/\n    &lt;chip_name&gt;/\n      &lt;board_name&gt;/\n        configs/nsh/defconfig\n        include/board.h\n        Kconfig\n        CMakeLists.txt\n        scripts/ld.script\n        scripts/Make.defs\n        src/ (board_boot.c, bringup.c, appinit.c, etc/)\n  chips/\n    &lt;chip_name&gt;/\n      chip.h\n      include/chip.h, irq.h\n      Kconfig\n      Make.defs\n      &lt;vendor&gt;_irq.c, _lowputc.c, _start.c, _timeisr.c\n```\n\n### 2. Required Files\n\n**Board-level files (mandatory):**\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `Kconfig` | Defines board configuration options. Must define a board config symbol like `ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_XXX_BOARD`. |\n| `CMakeLists.txt` | Top-level CMake file that adds `src/` subdirectory. |\n| `configs/nsh/defconfig` | The defconfig file specifying all kernel/driver/app configs. Must set `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y`, `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR`, and `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_NAME`. |\n| `src/board_boot.c` | Must implement `openvela_board_initialize()`. Optionally `board_early_initialize()`, `board_late_initialize()`, `board_app_initialize()`. |\n| `src/CMakeLists.txt` | Lists source files for the `board` library target using `nuttx_add_library(board)` and `target_sources()`. |\n| `scripts/ld.script` | Linker script defining memory layout (flash, SRAM regions). Entry point should be `_vectors`. |\n| `scripts/Make.defs` | Top-level build config: includes `.config`, `Config.mk`, toolchain defs, sets `LDSCRIPT`, `ARCHSCRIPT`, `CFLAGS`, `EXTRA_LIBS`. |\n| `include/board.h` | Board-specific macro definitions and function declarations. |\n\n**Chip-level files (if adding new SoC support):**\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/Kconfig` | Chip model selection, feature flags |\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/Make.defs` | Lists C source files for compilation |\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/&lt;vendor&gt;_start.c` | Reset entry point (`__start` function): clears BSS, copies .data, initializes clocks/serial, calls `nx_start()` |\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/&lt;vendor&gt;_irq.c` | Interrupt handling |\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/&lt;vendor&gt;_lowputc.c` | Low-level UART output |\n| `chips/&lt;chip&gt;/&lt;vendor&gt;_timeisr.c` | Timer ISR |\n\n### 3. Build System Organization\n\n**How the build system finds boards:**\n\nThe build system uses a `[vendor]-[board]-[config]` triple format. The `dump_build_choices()` function in `/home/warner/openvela/build/envsetup.sh` scans `vendor/*/boards/*/configs/*/` directories looking for both `CMakeLists.txt` and a `configs/` subdirectory.\n\n**Build commands:**\n\n```bash\n# Method 1: Direct build.sh invocation\n./build.sh vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_XXX_board/configs/nsh --cmake -j8\n\n# Method 2: Using envsetup.sh (recommended for CMake)\nsource build/envsetup.sh\nlunch [openvela]-[contest2026_XXX_board]-[nsh]\nm -j8\n```\n\n**Key defconfig settings** (from the vela/sil examples):\n\n```\nCONFIG_ARCH=\"arm\"                          # or \"riscv\", \"arm64\", etc.\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR=\"../vendor/openvela/boards/&lt;board_dir&gt;/\"\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR_RELPATH=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_NAME=\"&lt;config_name&gt;\"\nCONFIG_ARCH_CHIP=\"&lt;chip_name&gt;\"\nCONFIG_BOARD_EARLY_INITIALIZE=y\nCONFIG_BOARD_LATE_INITIALIZE=y\nCONFIG_ETC_ROMFS=y\nCONFIG_INIT_ENTRYPOINT=\"nsh_main\"\n```\n\n**Manifest linkage** (from the contest XML):\n\nThe team's `board/contest_board/` directory is symlinked into the build tree via:\n```xml\n&lt;linkfile src=\"board/contest_board\" dest=\"vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_XXX_board\"/&gt;\n```\n\nThis means the board appears at `vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_XXX_board/` in the openvela working tree, and the build system discovers it automatically.\n\n### 4. Specific Requirements for the \"新硬件适配\" Track\n\nFrom the contest overview (`/home/warner/openvela/demo/参赛相关/contest_overview (1).md`) and the porting guide (`/home/warner/openvela/docs/zh-cn/chip_porting/porting_guide.md`):\n\n**Track description:** \"将 openvela 移植到全新芯片/开发板，完成 BSP 适配与驱动开发\" (Port openvela to a new chip/development board, complete BSP adaptation and driver development).\n\n**Scoring criteria (100 total):**\n- Technical difficulty (30 pts): New chip adaptation, low-level driver extension, system architecture, deep openvela customization, hardware engineering capability\n- Product innovation (20 pts): Novelty in features/scenarios/AI interaction\n- Project completeness (20 pts): Working code + runnable demo + documentation, stable functionality\n- AI development (10 pts): AI-enabled development workflow, reusable Skills\n- Commercial potential (10 pts): Real application scenarios, scalable\n- Presentation (10 pts): Professional demo and defense\n\n**Minimum deliverables for hardware porting:**\n1. A working BSP with at least `nsh` (NuttShell) booting on the target hardware\n2. UART console driver working (serial output)\n3. Timer driver (arch_alarm or arch_timer model)\n4. Interrupt controller adaptation\n5. Memory/heap initialization\n6. A linker script matching the target hardware's memory map\n\n**The porting guide specifies a 3-layer adaptation model:**\n- Architecture layer (already supported by openvela -- ARM, RISC-V, etc.)\n- Chip/SoC layer (under `vendor/&lt;name&gt;/chips/`)\n- Board layer (under `vendor/&lt;name&gt;/boards/&lt;chip&gt;/&lt;board&gt;/`)\n\n**Build artifacts produced:**\n- `libarch.a` -- architecture static library\n- `libboards.a` -- board driver static library\n- `vela_nuttx.bin` -- final firmware binary for flashing\n\n**Testing:** The guide references an xTS test suite covering kernel, driver BSP, filesystem, WiFi, Bluetooth, audio/video capabilities. Teams should run both \"general self-test cases\" (mandatory: memory, scheduling, GPIO, I2C/SPI, UART, RTC, Watchdog) and \"category self-test cases\" (optional: WiFi, BT, LCD, Audio, FS, OTA).\n\n**Key files referenced:**\n- `/home/warner/openvela/docs/zh-cn/chip_porting/porting_guide.md` -- Full porting guide\n- `/home/warner/openvela/docs/zh-cn/chip_porting/Vendor.md` -- Vendor directory structure\n- `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/` -- Template board skeleton\n- `/home/warner/openvela/vendor/openvela/boards/sil/` -- Complete real board example (QEMU ARM32R)\n- `/home/warner/openvela/vendor/openvela/boards/vela/` -- Another real board example (QEMU goldfish)\n- `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/tools/build.sh` -- Main build script\n- `/home/warner/openvela/build/envsetup.sh` -- Build environment setup with `lunch`/`m` commands\n- `/home/warner/openvela/vendor/openvela/boards/build/vendorsetup.sh` -- Lunch combo registration</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>80254</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>56</tool_uses><duration_ms>189333</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:02:50.128Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"630088ec-b88d-42df-9fd0-aa51bb83d64e","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:02:50.128Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
