{"parentUuid":"b56a9c04-9696-4061-b21c-eed2cb2662bb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"081b7e96-06ec-419b-9b1e-d44e9d068e64","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user has two main goals:\n   - **Goal 1**: Configure FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader) for the nucleo-n657x0-q development board to make external XSPI flash work with power-off saving, referencing the mboot configuration in `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython`.\n   - **Goal 2**: Adapt the existing nucleo-n657x0-q NuttX board configuration into the contest board directory structure at `board/contest_board/` (which maps via manifest symlink to `vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board`) for the 2026 openvela AI Hardware Developer Contest \"新硬件适配\" (new hardware adaptation) track.\n   - **Goal 3**: Understand the manifest system, compilation methods, and how to git commit/push/PR to the contest repository.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - STM32N657X0 MCU (Cortex-M55, ARMv8.1-M) has NO internal flash - code must run from external XSPI flash (XIP) or SRAM\n   - XSPI2 peripheral interface with Macronix MX25UM51245G (512Mbit=64MB) flash chip\n   - XSPI pins: PN0-PN11 (AF9), VDDIO3 domain (1.8V)\n   - Boot flow: Hardware Boot ROM → FSBL (loaded to SRAM2 at 0x34180000, code starts at 0x34180400) → Main app (XIP at 0x70080000)\n   - Octal DTR (DOPI) mode for high-speed flash access\n   - Memory-mapped XIP at address 0x70000000\n   - BSEC OTP fuse for VDDIO3 high-speed IO optimization (one-time irreversible)\n   - openvela `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y` pattern for vendor boards\n   - repo manifest XML with `<linkfile>` for directory symlinks\n   - NuttX Kconfig build system with `arch/dummy/Kconfig` fallback mechanism\n   - STM32N6 chip support (`arch/arm/src/stm32n6/`) is MISSING from the current nuttx tree despite Kconfig defining it\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Reference files read (atk-dnn647-micropython)**:\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/mpconfigboard.h` - XSPI flash config: `MICROPY_HW_XSPIFLASH_SIZE_BITS_LOG2=28`, `MBOOT_SPIFLASH_ADDR=0x70000000`, pin definitions\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/board.c` - `mboot_board_early_init()` with VDDIO config, BSEC OTP fuse programming, `xspi_init()` call, PLL2/PLL4 setup\n   - `ports/stm32/xspi.c` - Complete XSPI2 driver with SPI/Octal DTR mode switching, memory-mapped XIP, QSPI protocol adapter\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/NUCLEO_N657X0/mpconfigboard.h` - MX25UM51245G config: `MICROPY_HW_XSPIFLASH_SIZE_BITS_LOG2=29`, 64MB flash\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/NUCLEO_N657X0/pins.csv` - XSPIM_P2 pin definitions (PN0-PN11)\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/NUCLEO_N657X0/board.c` - Simpler mboot_board_early_init (just config_vdd + xspi_init)\n   - `ports/stm32/boards/NUCLEO_N657X0/mpconfigboard.mk` - `USE_MBOOT=1`, `MCU_SERIES=n6`, FSBL system file, linker scripts\n\n   **Existing NuttX board files read**:\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/flash.ld` - SRAM-only linker script at 0x34000400, 4193280 bytes\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/include/board.h` - HSI 64MHz PLL config, CPU 200MHz, USART1 on PE5/PE6, LED definitions\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/configs/nsh/defconfig` - Standard NuttX board config\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/Make.defs` - Uses `armv8-m/Toolchain.defs`\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/src/` - stm32_boot.c, stm32_bringup.c, stm32_userleds.c, stm32_autoleds.c, nucleo-n657x0-q.h\n\n   **Contest files created/modified** (at `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/`):\n\n   - `Kconfig` - Board Kconfig with `ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD` guard\n     ```\n     if ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD\n     config ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD_TAG\n         string \"Board tag\"\n         default \"contest2026_224_board\"\n     endif\n     ```\n\n   - `configs/nsh/defconfig` - Main board configuration (evolved through multiple fixes):\n     ```\n     CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y\n     CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR=\"../vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board\"\n     CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR_RELPATH=y\n     CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_NAME=\"nsh\"\n     CONFIG_ARCH=\"arm\"\n     CONFIG_ARCH_ARMV8M=y\n     CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP=\"stm32n6\"\n     CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N6=y\n     CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N657X0=y\n     CONFIG_ARCH_INTERRUPTSTACK=4096\n     CONFIG_ARCH_STACKDUMP=y\n     CONFIG_BOARD_LATE_INITIALIZE=y\n     CONFIG_BOARD_LOOPSPERMSEC=21000\n     CONFIG_BUILTIN=y\n     CONFIG_HAVE_CXX=y\n     CONFIG_HAVE_CXXINITIALIZE=y\n     CONFIG_IDLETHREAD_STACKSIZE=4096\n     CONFIG_INIT_ENTRYPOINT=\"nsh_main\"\n     CONFIG_NSH_BUILTIN_APPS=y\n     CONFIG_NSH_FILEIOSIZE=512\n     CONFIG_NSH_READLINE=y\n     CONFIG_SYSTEM_NSH=y\n     CONFIG_RAM_START=0x34000400\n     CONFIG_RAM_SIZE=4193280\n     CONFIG_RAW_BINARY=y\n     CONFIG_RR_INTERVAL=200\n     CONFIG_SCHED_WAITPID=y\n     CONFIG_STM32_USART1=y\n     CONFIG_USART1_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y\n     CONFIG_STACK_USAGE_WARNING=0\n     CONFIG_DEBUG_FEATURES=y\n     CONFIG_DEBUG_ERROR=y\n     CONFIG_DEBUG_WARN=y\n     ```\n\n   - `include/board.h` - Clock tree (HSI 64MHz, PLL1, CPU 200MHz, HCLK 50MHz), LED definitions (LD5 PG10 Red, LD6 PG0 Green, LD7 PG8 Blue), USART1 pins, VDDIO config\n\n   - `scripts/flash.ld` - SRAM-only linker script: `sram (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x34000400, LENGTH = 4193280`\n\n   - `scripts/Make.defs` - ARMv8-M toolchain with PATH addition:\n     ```makefile\n     include ${TOPDIR}/.config\n     include ${TOPDIR}/tools/Config.mk\n     PREBUILT_GCC := $(TOPDIR)/../prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/arm-none-eabi/bin\n     ifneq ($(PATH),)\n       export PATH := $(PREBUILT_GCC):$(PATH)\n     endif\n     include ${TOPDIR}/arch/arm/src/armv8-m/Toolchain.defs\n     ARCHSCRIPT += $(BOARD_DIR)$(DELIM)scripts$(DELIM)flash.ld\n     ```\n\n   - `src/CMakeLists.txt`, `src/Make.defs` - Build config for source files\n   - `src/contest_board.h` - LED GPIO definitions (GPIO_LD5, GPIO_LD6, GPIO_LD7)\n   - `src/stm32_boot.c` - `stm32_board_initialize()`, `board_late_initialize()`, `board_app_initialize()`\n   - `src/stm32_bringup.c` - `stm32_bringup()` with userled registration\n   - `src/stm32_userleds.c` - User LED control (board_userled_initialize, board_userled, board_userled_all)\n   - `src/stm32_autoleds.c` - Auto LED control for OS events\n   - `README.md` - Board documentation with hardware info, build instructions, file structure\n\n   **Files created for build system fix**:\n   - `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/dummy/dummy_kconfig` - Empty placeholder (0 bytes)\n   - `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/boards/dummy/dummy_kconfig` - Empty placeholder (0 bytes)\n\n   **Guide file created**:\n   - `/home/warner/openvela/nucleo-n657x0-q-fsbl-guide.md` - Comprehensive 8-step guide for FSBL + XSPI flash configuration\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Files written to wrong directory**: Initially created board files at `board/NUCLEO-N657X0-Q/` instead of `board/contest_board/`. Fixed by `mv board/NUCLEO-N657X0-Q board/contest_board`.\n   \n   - **Broken symlink**: Manifest created symlink at `vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board -> ../../contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board` but relative path was wrong (one level off). Fixed by `rm` and recreating with `../../../contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board`.\n   \n   - **`arch/dummy` missing error**: Build system's `Config.mk` sets `CHIP_KCONFIG = arch/dummy/dummy_kconfig` for non-custom chips, but file didn't exist. Fixed by creating empty `arch/dummy/dummy_kconfig` and `boards/dummy/dummy_kconfig` files.\n   \n   - **ARM toolchain not found**: `arm-none-eabi-gcc` not in PATH. Located at `/home/warner/openvela/prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86_64/arm-none-eabi/bin/`. Added PATH export 