{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:17:53.954Z","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a902151a12d2806fd</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_d38fcc45ecba47f6990c9ce8</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-warner-openvela/2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3/tasks/a902151a12d2806fd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore contest_board structure\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Here is the complete analysis of the contest_board directory structure and what needs to be added/modified for FSBL and XSPI flash support.\n\n---\n\n## Complete File Listing and Purposes\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n```\ncontest_board/\n├── CMakeLists.txt\n├── Kconfig\n├── README.md\n├── configs/\n│   └── nsh/\n│       └── defconfig\n├── include/\n│   └── board.h\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── flash.ld\n│   └── Make.defs\n└── src/\n    ├── CMakeLists.txt\n    ├── Make.defs\n    ├── contest_board.h\n    ├── stm32_autoleds.c\n    ├── stm32_boot.c\n    ├── stm32_bringup.c\n    └── stm32_userleds.c\n```\n\n### Symlink\n\n`/home/warner/openvela/vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board` is a symlink pointing to `../../../contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board` (i.e., the same directory above). This is how the NuttX build system discovers the custom board via `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR`.\n\n---\n\n## File-by-File Analysis\n\n### 1. Top-Level CMakeLists.txt\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/CMakeLists.txt`\n\nMinimal file -- just calls `add_subdirectory(src)`. No board-specific logic beyond delegating to src/.\n\n### 2. Kconfig\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/Kconfig`\n\nDefines a single config option `ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD_TAG` (string, default \"contest2026_224_board\"). Guarded by `if ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD`. Does not yet define any FSBL or XSPI-related Kconfig options.\n\n### 3. README.md\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/README.md`\n\nDocuments the hardware (STM32N657X0, Cortex-M55, 200MHz, MX25UM51245G XSPI2 flash, 4MB AXI SRAM, USART1 on PE5/PE6, three LEDs on PG0/PG8/PG10). The \"To Do\" section explicitly lists the missing pieces:\n- XSPI driver (`stm32n6_xspi.c`)\n- VDDIO3 power domain configuration (1.8V for XSPI pins)\n- BSEC OTP fuse configuration (high-speed IO optimization)\n- FSBL (first stage boot loader)\n- XIP linker script (`0x70080000`)\n- Flash partition and MTD driver\n- LittleFS power-loss-safe storage\n\n### 4. include/board.h\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/include/board.h`\n\nDefines:\n- **Clock tree:** HSI 64MHz / M=4 * N=50 = 800MHz VCO, IC1/4 = 200MHz CPU clock, HCLK=50MHz, PCLK1/PCLK2=50MHz\n- **Power domains:** `BOARD_PWR_VDDIO` configures VDDIO2 and VDDIO3 for 1.8V (for USART1 on PE5/PE6)\n- **LEDs:** LD5=PG10 (Red), LD6=PG0 (Green), LD7=PG8 (Blue), active LOW\n- **USART1 pins:** PE5=TX (AF7), PE6=RX (AF7)\n\n**What needs modification for XSPI:** XSPI2 pins on port N (PN0-PN12) use AF9 and require VDDIO3 at 1.8V. The `BOARD_PWR_VDDIO` already sets VDDIO3SV and VDDIO3VRSEL, but pin configuration for XSPI2 (PN0-PN12) is not present. Also, no XSPI-related clock or memory map definitions exist yet.\n\n### 5. scripts/flash.ld\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/scripts/flash.ld`\n\nSRAM-only linker script for DEV boot mode. Single memory region:\n- `sram (rwx): ORIGIN = 0x34180400, LENGTH = 0x80000` (512KB SRAM2)\n\nEverything (.text, .data, .bss) goes into this single SRAM region. There is no flash memory region defined.\n\n**What needs to be added for FSBL/XSPI:** A new linker script (e.g., `xip.ld`) needs to be created with at least two memory regions:\n- `sram2` for FSBL code at `0x34180400` (where boot ROM loads the FSBL)\n- `ext_flash (rx)` at `0x70080000` for XIP application code (the NuttX kernel)\n\nThe MicroPython reference at `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/stm32n657x0.ld` shows the pattern: `SRAM2_S_FSBL` at `0x34180400` (511K) for the FSBL, and `EXT_FLASH` at `0x70080000` (1536K) for the application.\n\n### 6. scripts/Make.defs\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/scripts/Make.defs`\n\nConfigures the ARMv8-M toolchain (Cortex-M55), adds the openvela prebuilt GCC to PATH, includes `armv8-m/Toolchain.defs`, and sets `ARCHSCRIPT` to `scripts/flash.ld`. Standard CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS/AFLAGS setup.\n\n**What needs modification for FSBL:** If adding a second linker script for XIP, this file would need to conditionally select between `flash.ld` (DEV mode) and the new `xip.ld` (FSBL+XIP mode) based on a Kconfig option.\n\n### 7. src/CMakeLists.txt\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/CMakeLists.txt`\n\nSets SRCS to `stm32_boot.c stm32_bringup.c`, conditionally adds `stm32_autoleds.c` (if `CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS`) or `stm32_userleds.c`. Sets LD_SCRIPT to `flash.ld`.\n\n**What needs modification for XSPI:** New source files (XSPI driver, FSBL initialization) need to be added to the SRCS list, and the LD_SCRIPT property may need to change conditionally.\n\n### 8. src/Make.defs\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/Make.defs`\n\nMakefile version of the CMakeLists.txt above. Lists `CSRCS = stm32_boot.c stm32_bringup.c` plus conditional LED sources.\n\n### 9. src/contest_board.h\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/contest_board.h`\n\nPrivate board header. Defines GPIO pin configurations for LD5 (PG10), LD6 (PG0), LD7 (PG8) using STM32 GPIO macros. Declares `stm32_bringup()`.\n\n**What needs to be added for XSPI:** XSPI2 pin definitions (PN0-PN12 as AF9, very high speed) and any XSPI-related constants.\n\n### 10. src/stm32_boot.c\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_boot.c`\n\nImplements `stm32_board_initialize()` -- currently contains an infinite LED blink loop (LD6 green at ~1Hz) as a \"CPU alive\" indicator. Also implements `board_late_initialize()` and `board_app_initialize()` which both call `stm32_bringup()`.\n\n**Critical note:** The infinite blink loop in `stm32_board_initialize()` will prevent the system from ever booting past this point. This is clearly a debug/test artifact that needs to be removed or gated behind a config option before real operation.\n\n**What needs modification for FSBL:** The FSBL's `SystemInit()` equivalent would need to be called very early (before NuttX starts). In FSBL mode, `stm32_board_initialize()` would need to configure XSPI2, set up memory-mapped mode, and then jump to the application in external flash -- or for NuttX-as-FSBL, it would configure XSPI and then continue NuttX initialization with XIP from flash.\n\n### 11. src/stm32_bringup.c\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_bringup.c`\n\nMinimal -- only registers the user LED driver at `/dev/userleds` if `CONFIG_USERLED_LOWER` is set and `CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS` is not set.\n\n**What needs to be added for XSPI:** After XSPI initialization, this function should register the flash as an MTD device, set up flash partitions, and optionally mount LittleFS.\n\n### 12. src/stm32_autoleds.c and src/stm32_userleds.c\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_autoleds.c` and `stm32_userleds.c`\n\nStandard NuttX LED drivers for the three on-board LEDs. These are complete and functional. No changes needed for FSBL/XSPI.\n\n### 13. configs/nsh/defconfig\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/configs/nsh/defconfig`\n\nKey settings:\n- `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y` with custom dir pointing to vendor board\n- `CONFIG_ARCH=\"arm\"`, `CONFIG_ARCH_ARMV8M=y`, `CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N657X0=y`\n- `CONFIG_RAM_START=0x34180400`, `CONFIG_RAM_SIZE=0x80000` (512KB SRAM2)\n- `CONFIG_STM32_USART1=y`, `CONFIG_USART1_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y`\n- `CONFIG_BOARD_LATE_INITIALIZE=y`\n- NSH shell configured as init entry point\n\n**What needs to be added for FSBL/XSPI:** New Kconfig options would need to be enabled, such as:\n- `CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI2=y` (XSPI2 peripheral driver)\n- `CONFIG_FSBL=y` or similar (FSBL boot mode)\n- `CONFIG_MTD=y`, `CONFIG_MTD_PARTITION=y` (flash partitions)\n- `CONFIG_FS_LITTLEFS=y` (if using LittleFS)\n- `CONFIG_RAM_START` and memory layout changes for XIP mode\n\n---\n\n## Reference Files Examined\n\n### MicroPython FSBL Reference\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c`\n\nA complete XSPI2 driver for the MX25UM51245G flash on XSPI2. Key details:\n- Uses XSPI2 instance, pins PN0-PN12, AF9\n- XIP base address: `0x70000000` for XSPI2\n- Supports both SPI (1-line) and DTR octal (8-line) modes\n- Memory-mapped mode for XIP with `FMODE=3`\n- `xspi_init()` configures XSPIM in direct mode, sets up XSPI2 registers (Macronix memory type, prescaler, chip select timing)\n- `xspi_switch_to_dtr()` sends WREN then writes config register 0x00000000 with value 2 to enter DOPI DTR mode\n\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/tinyusb/hw/bsp/stm32n6/boards/stm32n657nucleo/STM32N657XX_AXISRAM2_fsbl.ld`\n\nFSBL linker script: ROM at `0x34180400` (255K) for code, RAM at `0x341C0000` (256K) for data/bss. Entry point is `Reset_Handler`.\n\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/stm32lib/CMSIS/STM32N6xx/Source/Templates/gcc/startup_stm32n657xx_fsbl.s`\n\nFSBL startup assembly for GCC. Sets stack pointer, calls `SystemInit()`, copies .data from flash to SRAM, zeros .bss, calls `__libc_init_array`, then `main()`.\n\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/stm32lib/CMSIS/STM32N6xx/Source/Templates/system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c`\n\nFSBL system init. Key operations:\n- Sets VTOR to the vector table location\n- Clears SAU regions (TrustZone)\n- Resets XSPI2 and XSPIM peripherals\n- Configures power clamps and VREF\n- Sets up FPU\n\n### Upstream NuttX Board\n**Path:** `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/`\n\nThe upstream NuttX board is also SRAM-only (DEV mode). Its linker script places everything at `0x34000400` with 4MB length. There are no existing XSPI or FSBL files in the NuttX STM32N6 arch directory (`/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/`).\n\n---\n\n## Summary: What Needs to Be Added/Modified for FSBL and XSPI Flash Support\n\n### New Files to Create\n\n1. **`src/stm32_xspi.c`** -- XSPI2 driver for MX25UM51245G flash. Based on the MicroPython reference at `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c`. Needs to configure XSPI2 peripheral, set up memory-mapped mode for XIP at `0x70080000`, and provide read/write/erase functions for MTD.\n\n2. **`scripts/xip.ld`** (or `flash_xip.ld`) -- Linker script for FSBL+XIP mode. Needs two memory regions: SRAM2 at `0x34180400` for FSBL code and data, and external flash at `0x70080000` for the NuttX application (XIP). The `.text` and `.rodata` sections go to flash; `.data` and `.bss` go to SRAM.\n\n3. **`src/stm32_fsbl.c`** (optional) -- FSBL initialization code. Configures XSPI2, sets up memory-mapped mode, and optionally loads/copies the application from flash to SRAM if not doing pure XIP. Alternatively, this logic can be integrated into `stm32_boot.c`.\n\n4. **`src/stm32_flash_mtd.c`** (optional) -- Flash partition and MTD driver registration for block-level access to the XSPI flash (needed for LittleFS).\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n1. **`include/board.h`** -- Add XSPI2 pin definitions (PN0-PN12, AF9), XSPI clock configuration, and XIP base address define (`0x70080000`).\n\n2. **`src/contest_board.h`** -- Add XSPI2 GPIO pin macros and any XSPI-related constants.\n\n3. **`src/stm32_boot.c`** -- Remove or gate the infinite LED blink loop. Add FSBL initialization sequence (XSPI2 setup, memory-mapped mode enable) before NuttX continues. The `SystemInit()` from the FSBL reference (`system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c`) shows the required early hardware init (VTOR, SAU clear, XSPI2/XSPIM reset, power config).\n\n4. **`src/stm32_bringup.c`** -- Add XSPI flash MTD registration, partition setup, and optionally LittleFS mount.\n\n5. **`src/CMakeLists.txt`** -- Add new source files (`stm32_xspi.c`, etc.) to SRCS. Conditionally select linker script based on FSBL/XIP config.\n\n6. **`src/Make.defs`** -- Same as CMakeLists.txt changes (Make build system).\n\n7. **`scripts/Make.defs`** -- Conditionally select between `flash.ld` (DEV mode) and `xip.ld` (FSBL+XIP mode).\n\n8. **`Kconfig`** -- Add config options for XSPI driver, FSBL boot mode, XIP vs SRAM-only, flash partitions, LittleFS, etc.\n\n9. **`configs/nsh/defconfig`** -- Enable new options: `CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI2=y`, `CONFIG_MTD=y`, memory layout changes for XIP, etc.\n\n10. **`CMakeLists.txt`** (top-level) -- May need no changes if all new logic is in `src/CMakeLists.txt`.\n\n### Key Hardware Details for Implementation\n\n- **XSPI2 base address:** `0x70000000` (XIP window); application starts at `0x70080000` (offset 512KB, after FSBL's reserved area in flash)\n- **XSPI2 pins:** PN0-PN12, AF9, very high speed\n- **Flash chip:** MX25UM51245G, 512Mbit (64MB), Macronix mode in XSPI DCR1\n- **Boot flow:** Boot ROM loads FSBL into SRAM2 at `0x34180400`; FSBL configures XSPI2 and enables memory-mapped mode; then either jumps to XIP application or (in NuttX's case) continues NuttX initialization with code running from flash\n- **Power domain:** VDDIO3 must be 1.8V for XSPI pins (already partially configured in `BOARD_PWR_VDDIO`)\n- **NuttX STM32N6 arch:** Currently has no XSPI driver at `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/` -- the board-level code will need to provide the driver or the arch layer needs to be extended</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>56108</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>33</tool_uses><duration_ms>127301</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
