{"parentUuid":"41cd6e12-8049-40a9-ac3c-7141da5ff855","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_3665a480fd6a49b9a74ec51a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_03809a6723c843fea7ef0b94","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/warner/.claude/plans/wild-brewing-storm.md","content":"# FSBL + XSPI Flash Implementation Plan\n\n## Context\n\nSTM32N657X0 has NO internal flash. Code must run from external XSPI flash (XIP) or SRAM. The current NuttX build only supports SRAM mode (DEV boot via debugger). To make the board production-ready with power-off persistence, we need:\n\n1. **XSPI driver** - Initialize XSPI2 peripheral, switch flash to Octal DTR mode, enable memory-mapped XIP\n2. **FSBL** - First Stage Boot Loader that runs from SRAM2, initializes XSPI, jumps to main app at 0x70080000\n3. **XIP linker script** - Link main app to run from external flash at 0x70080000\n\nReference: `/home/warner/openvela/demo/nucleo-n657x0-q-fsbl-guide.md` and `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c`\n\n## Files to Create/Modify\n\nAll work targets the **contest_board** at `/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/`\n\n### Phase 1: XSPI Hardware Register Definitions\n\n**NEW: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h`**\n- XSPI register offsets (CR, DCR1-4, SR, FCR, DLR, DR, IR, AR, TCR, CCR, LPTR)\n- XSPI bit field definitions (CR_EN, CR_FMODE, SR_BUSY, SR_TCF, SR_FTF, SR_TEF, etc.)\n- XSPIM register definitions (CR)\n- Based on RM0486 reference manual\n\n### Phase 2: XSPI Driver\n\n**NEW: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.h`**\n- Public API: `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()`, memory-mapped enable/exit\n\n**NEW: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c`**\n- Pin configuration (PN0-PN11, AF9, VERY_HIGH speed)\n- Clock enable (AHB5: XSPIM, XSPI1, XSPI2)\n- XSPIM direct mode setup\n- XSPI2 peripheral configuration (DCR1: Macronix type, 64MB, CSHT; DCR2: prescaler)\n- Flash reset sequence (SPI mode)\n- Octal DTR mode switching (WREN -> RDSR poll WEL -> WRSCUR 0x02)\n- Memory-mapped XIP enable (8-line DTR, 20 dummy cycles, FMODE=3)\n- Memory-mapped exit (abort, wait BUSY)\n- Reference: `atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c`\n\n### Phase 3: FSBL\n\n**NEW: `contest_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c`**\n- Entry at 0x34180400 (loaded by boot ROM from flash offset 0)\n- Set VTOR to 0x34180400\n- Configure VDDIO3 (1.8V) for XSPI pins\n- Program BSEC OTP fuse for HSLV (one-time, optional)\n- Call `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()`\n- Jump to main app at 0x70080000 (read SP and PC from vector table)\n\n**NEW: `contest_board/scripts/fsbl.ld`**\n- fsbl_code: ORIGIN = 0x34180400, LENGTH = 31KB\n- fsbl_ram: ORIGIN = 0x341E0000, LENGTH = 128KB\n\n**NEW: `contest_board/configs/fsbl/defconfig`**\n- Minimal config: no NSH, no apps, just enough to init XSPI and jump\n- CONFIG_STM32N6_FSBL=y\n\n### Phase 4: XIP Linker Script\n\n**NEW: `contest_board/scripts/xip.ld`**\n- flash (rx): ORIGIN = 0x70080000, LENGTH = 8MB\n- sram (rwx): ORIGIN = 0x34000400, LENGTH = 4MB\n- .text/.rodata -> flash, .data/.bss -> sram\n\n**NEW: `contest_board/configs/xip/defconfig`**\n- Full NSH config but linked for XIP from flash\n- CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI=y\n\n### Phase 5: Pin Definitions and Board Integration\n\n**MODIFY: `contest_board/include/board.h`**\n- Add XSPI2 pin definitions (GPIO_XSPI2_DQS/CS/IO0-IO7/SCK)\n- These need to be defined as raw GPIO macros since NuttX pinmap.h doesn't have them yet\n\n**MODIFY: `contest_board/src/stm32_bringup.c`**\n- Add `#ifdef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI` block to call `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()`\n\n**MODIFY: `contest_board/src/Make.defs` and `contest_board/src/CMakeLists.txt`**\n- Add stm32_fsbl.c conditionally for FSBL config\n- Add stm32n6_xspi.c reference (from arch dir)\n\n### Phase 6: Kconfig\n\n**MODIFY: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Kconfig`**\n- Add `STM32N6_XSPI` bool option\n- Add `STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER` int option (default 4)\n- Add `STM32N6_FSBL` bool option\n\n**MODIFY: `contest_board/Kconfig`**\n- Add board-specific XSPI options if needed\n\n### Phase 7: Build System\n\n**MODIFY: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Make.defs`**\n- Add `stm32n6_xspi.c` conditionally for CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI\n\n**MODIFY: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/CMakeLists.txt`**\n- Same conditional addition\n\n## Key Technical Details\n\n### XSPI2 Pin Mapping (PN0-PN11, AF9, VDDIO3 1.8V)\n| Pin | Function | GPIO Macro |\n|-----|----------|------------|\n| PN0 | DQS | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN0 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN1 | CS | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN1 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN2 | IO0 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN2 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN3 | IO1 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN3 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN4 | IO2 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN4 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN5 | IO3 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN5 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN6 | SCK | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN6 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN8 | IO4 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN8 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN9 | IO5 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN9 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN10 | IO6 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN10 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n| PN11 | IO7 | GPIO_PORTN \\| GPIO_PIN11 \\| GPIO_AF9 \\| GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH |\n\n### Flash Layout\n| Offset | Size | Content |\n|--------|------|---------|\n| 0x000000 | 512KB | FSBL (signed) |\n| 0x080000 | 8MB | Main NuttX app (XIP) |\n| 0x880000 | ~55MB | Filesystem / data |\n\n### Build Commands\n```bash\n# FSBL\ncmake -B build_fsbl -DBOARD_CONFIG=contest2026_224_board:fsbl -S .\ncmake --build build_fsbl -j8\n\n# Main app (XIP)\ncmake -B build_xip -DBOARD_CONFIG=contest2026_224_board:xip -S .\ncmake --build build_xip -j8\n```\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Build FSBL - should produce nuttx.bin linked at 0x34180400\n2. Build XIP app - should produce nuttx.bin linked at 0x70080000\n3. Flash FSBL to external flash offset 0 (via STM32CubeProgrammer + external loader)\n4. Flash main app to external flash offset 0x080000\n5. Reset board - should boot through FSBL into NuttX NSH shell\n6. Verify XIP by checking code runs from 0x70080000 address space\n"}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":2128,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":120192}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"ff6946cb-7f78-4bf5-80b7-88e1b3518624","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:19:17.089Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
