{"parentUuid":"213ee055-886b-48c8-9ab6-c2d2241f06e6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3891a978-26cd-4836-9ded-b78472f3701e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user has three main goals:\n   - **Goal 1**: Configure FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader) for the nucleo-n657x0-q development board to make external XSPI flash work with power-off saving, referencing the mboot configuration in `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython`.\n   - **Goal 2**: Adapt the existing nucleo-n657x0-q NuttX board configuration into the contest board directory structure at `board/contest_board/` (mapping via manifest symlink to `vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board`) for the 2026 openvela AI Hardware Developer Contest.\n   - **Goal 3**: Understand the manifest system, compilation methods, and how to git commit/push/PR to the contest repository.\n   \n   In this session, the user explicitly asked to: (a) fix the build so contest_board compiles, (b) explain NuttX vs openvela firmware differences, (c) explain how to test board flashing, and (d) implement FSBL based on the guide document and reference code.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - STM32N657X0 MCU (Cortex-M55, ARMv8.1-M) has NO internal flash - code runs from external XSPI flash (XIP) or SRAM\n   - XSPI2 peripheral interface with Macronix MX25UM51245G (512Mbit=64MB) flash chip\n   - XSPI pins: PN0-PN11 (AF9), VDDIO3 domain (1.8V)\n   - Boot flow: Hardware Boot ROM → FSBL (loaded to SRAM2 at 0x34180000, code starts at 0x34180400) → Main app (XIP at 0x70080000)\n   - Octal DTR (DOPI) mode for high-speed flash access\n   - Memory-mapped XIP at address 0x70000000\n   - openvela `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM=y` pattern for vendor boards\n   - CMake build system with kconfiglib (Python-based Kconfig parser supporting `osource`)\n   - NuttX is the RTOS kernel; openvela is a complete IoT OS built on top of NuttX\n   - `select` cannot be used on choice symbols in Kconfig (ARCH_CHIP_STM32 is a choice symbol)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Created: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h`**\n   - XSPI hardware register definitions for STM32N6\n   - Register offsets (CR, DCR1-4, SR, FCR, DLR, CCR, TCR, IR, AR, DR, LPTR)\n   - Bit field definitions for all registers\n   - XSPI register structure (xspi_regs_t) and XSPIM structure (xspim_regs_t)\n   - RCC AHB5 enable/reset bits for XSPI\n   - Includes XSPI_CR_EN_Pos definition that was initially missing\n\n   **Created: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.h`**\n   - XSPI driver public API header\n   - Defines `STM32N6_XSPI2_XIP_BASE` (0x70000000), flash size constants\n   - Function prototypes: `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()`, `stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit()`, `stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable()`\n\n   **Created: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c`**\n   - Full XSPI2 driver implementation ported from MicroPython reference\n   - Pin configuration using raw GPIO macros: `GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PINx | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL | GPIO_SPEED_100MHZ`\n   - Clock enable via AHB5 registers\n   - XSPIM direct mode setup\n   - SPI mode read/write (111 mode)\n   - Octal DTR mode switching: WREN → RDSR poll WEL → WRSCUR 0x02\n   - Memory-mapped XIP: 8-line DTR, 20 dummy cycles, FMODE=3\n   - Memory-mapped exit: abort, wait BUSY, set FMODE=0\n\n   **Created: `contest_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c`**\n   - FSBL entry point at 0x34180400\n   - Sets VTOR, configures VDDIO3 (1.8V), calls `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()`\n   - Jumps to main app at 0x70080000 (reads SP and PC from vector table)\n   - Uses `__asm__ volatile (\"msr msp, %0\")` to set stack pointer\n   - Includes `arm_m_nvic.h` for SCB definition (currently failing)\n\n   **Created: `contest_board/scripts/fsbl.ld`**\n   - FSBL linker script: fsbl_code at 0x34180400 (31KB), fsbl_ram at 0x341E0000 (128KB)\n\n   **Created: `contest_board/scripts/xip.ld`**\n   - XIP linker script: flash at 0x70080000 (8MB), sram at 0x34000400 (4MB)\n   - .text/.rodata → flash, .data/.bss → sram (data load address in flash)\n\n   **Created: `contest_board/configs/fsbl/defconfig`**\n   - Minimal config for FSBL: no NSH, no apps, RAM at 0x34180400 (31KB)\n   - CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI=y, CONFIG_STM32N6_FSBL=y\n\n   **Created: `contest_board/configs/xip/defconfig`**\n   - Full NSH config linked for XIP: RAM at 0x34000400, USART1 console\n   - CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI=y (no FSBL flag)\n\n   **Modified: `contest_board/include/board.h`**\n   - Added XSPI2 pin documentation comment block\n\n   **Modified: `contest_board/Kconfig`**\n   - Changed guard from `if ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD` to `if ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM`\n   - Added `STM32N6_XSPI` bool, `STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER` int, `STM32N6_FSBL` bool\n\n   **Modified: `contest_board/src/stm32_bringup.c`**\n   - Added `#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"` under `CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI`\n   - Added `stm32n6_xspi_initialize()` call in bringup function\n\n   **Modified: `contest_board/src/Make.defs`**\n   - Added `stm32_fsbl.c` conditionally for CONFIG_STM32N6_FSBL\n\n   **Modified: `contest_board/src/CMakeLists.txt`**\n   - Added stm32_fsbl.c conditionally\n   - Added linker script selection: fsbl.ld for FSBL, xip.ld for XSPI, flash.ld for default\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Make.defs`**\n   - Added `stm32n6_xspi.c` conditionally for CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI\n   - stm32_serial.c is unconditionally included (CONFIG_STM32_USART not available)\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/CMakeLists.txt`**\n   - Added stm32n6_xspi.c conditionally\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/arch/arm/Kconfig`**\n   - Added `config ARCH_CHIP_STM32N6` (without `select ARCH_CHIP_STM32` since it's a choice symbol)\n   - Added `default \"stm32n6\" if ARCH_CHIP_STM32N6`\n   - Added `source \"arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Kconfig\"` block\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h`**\n   - Added `STM32_XSPI1_BASE 0x58029000`\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h`**\n   - Added `STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR_OFFSET 0x0260` and `STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR_OFFSET 0x0264`\n   - Added `STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR` and `STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR` register addresses\n\n   **Modified: `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_boot.c`**\n   - Added `board_app_initialize()` stub under CONFIG_BOARDCTL\n\n   **Created symlinks:**\n   - `nuttx/arch/arm/include/armv8-m -> arm_m`\n   - `nuttx/include/nuttx/debug.h -> ../debug.h`\n   - `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/contest2026_224_board -> /home/warner/openvela/vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **stm32n6 chip source missing**: `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/` directory didn't exist on `feature/add_stm32n6` branch. Fixed by `git checkout upstream/master -- arch/arm/src/stm32n6/` and related directories.\n   \n   - **arch/arm/Kconfig missing STM32N6 entries**: Manually added config, default, and source entries for STM32N6.\n   \n   - **armv8-m include directory missing**: `arch/arm/include/armv8-m` didn't exist. Fixed with symlink to `arm_m`.\n   \n   - **nuttx/debug.h missing**: Code included `<nuttx/debug.h>` but file was at `include/debug.h`. Fixed with symlink `include/nuttx/debug.h -> ../debug.h`.\n   \n   - **stm32_serial.c not compiled**: `CONFIG_STM32_USART` not set because common STM32 Kconfig not sourced (ARCH_CHIP_STM32 is choice symbol, can't be selected). Fixed by making stm32_serial.c unconditionally compiled in Make.defs and CMakeLists.txt.\n   \n   - **board_app_initialize undefined**: Upstream board didn't have this function. Added empty stub.\n   \n   - **Kconfig syntax errors in openvela**: Pre-existing errors in frameworks/runtimes/quickapp/Kconfig (`--help--` instead of `---help---`). Fixed with sed.\n   \n   - **CMake can't find kconfiglib**: System kconfig-conf doesn't support `osource`. Fixed by using openvela's kconfiglib: `PATH=/home/warner/openvela/prebuilts/tools/python/bin:$PATH` and `PYTHONPATH=/home/warner/openvela/prebuilts/tools/python/dist-packages:/home/warner/openvela/prebuilts/tools/python/dist-packages/kconfiglib`.\n   \n   - **Ninja not found**: CMake defaulted to Ninja generator. Fixed by using Unix Makefiles (default).\n   \n   - **ARCH_BOARD_CONTEST2026_224_BOARD not defined**: Kconfig guard symbol not recognized. Fixed by changing guard to `if ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM`.\n   \n   - **GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH undeclared**: NuttX uses `GPIO_SPEED_100MHZ` (value 3). Fixed in stm32n6_xspi.c.\n   \n   - **STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR/AHB5ENR undeclared**: Not defined in RCC header. Added offset and address definitions to stm32n6xxx_rcc.h.\n   \n   - **STM32_XSPI1_BASE undeclared**: Not in memorymap.h. Added `0x58029000`.\n   \n   - **STM32_RCC_APB4ENR2 undeclared**: Should be `STM32_RCC_APB4HENR`. Fixed in stm32_fsbl.c.\n   \n   - **XSPI_CR_EN_Pos undeclared**: Missing position macro. Added to stm32n6xxx_xspi.h.\n   \n   - **SCB undeclared in stm32_fsbl.c**: Added `#include \"arm_m_nvic.h\"`. **THIS IS STILL FAILING** - the header path may be wrong.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Solved**: nucleo-n657x0-q board builds successfully (nuttx.bin 72KB, ARM Cortex-M55 ELF)\n   - **Solved**: contest_board builds successfully in nsh configuration (nuttx.bin 73KB)\n   - **Solved**: Kconfig system works with openvela's kconfiglib Python package\n   - **In Progress**: FSBL build failing with `arm_m_nvic.h: No such file or directory`\n   - **Not Started**: XIP configuration build\n   - **Not Started**: Actual hardware testing\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"继续\" (continue - after interrupting a tool use)\n   - \"nuttx中编译的系统和openvela编译出来的固件是否一样，烧录了nuttx的固件之后，openvela是怎么实现的\" (asking about NuttX vs openvela firmware differences)\n   - \"先帮我把 contest_board 也编译通过\" (first help me get contest_board to compile)\n   - \"怎么测试板子实际烧录之后的运行情况\" (how to test the board after actual flashing)\n   -