{"parentUuid":"5f687f87-9a62-42d1-af05-f8de7d7dbfc1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h","content":"/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\n * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\n * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.\n * The ASF licenses this file to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n * (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with\n * the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\n *\n *   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n *\n * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n * WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n * See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n * limitations under the License.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#ifndef __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_XSPI_H\n#define __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_XSPI_H\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* XSPI register offsets ****************************************************/\n\n#define XSPI_CR_OFFSET      0x0000  /* Control register */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_OFFSET    0x0008  /* Device configuration register 1 */\n#define XSPI_DCR2_OFFSET    0x000C  /* Device configuration register 2 */\n#define XSPI_DCR3_OFFSET    0x0010  /* Device configuration register 3 */\n#define XSPI_DCR4_OFFSET    0x0014  /* Device configuration register 4 */\n#define XSPI_SR_OFFSET      0x0020  /* Status register */\n#define XSPI_FCR_OFFSET     0x0024  /* Flag clear register */\n#define XSPI_DLR_OFFSET     0x0040  /* Data length register */\n#define XSPI_CCR_OFFSET     0x0100  /* Communication configuration register */\n#define XSPI_TCR_OFFSET     0x0108  /* Timing configuration register */\n#define XSPI_IR_OFFSET      0x0110  /* Instruction register */\n#define XSPI_ABR_OFFSET     0x0118  /* Alternate bytes register */\n#define XSPI_AR_OFFSET      0x0120  /* Address register */\n#define XSPI_DR_OFFSET      0x0130  /* Data register */\n#define XSPI_MSKSR_OFFSET   0x0134  /* Masked status register */\n#define XSPI_LPTR_OFFSET    0x0144  /* Low-power timeout register */\n\n/* XSPI Control Register (CR) ***********************************************/\n\n#define XSPI_CR_EN_Pos          0\n#define XSPI_CR_EN              (1 << 0)   /* Enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_ABORT_Pos       1\n#define XSPI_CR_ABORT           (1 << 1)   /* Abort request */\n#define XSPI_CR_DMAEN_Pos       2\n#define XSPI_CR_DMAEN           (1 << 2)   /* DMA enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_TCEN_Pos        3\n#define XSPI_CR_TCEN            (1 << 3)   /* Timeout counter enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_DMM_Pos         6\n#define XSPI_CR_DMM             (1 << 6)   /* Dual-memory mode */\n#define XSPI_CR_CSSEL_Pos       8\n#define XSPI_CR_CSSEL           (1 << 8)   /* Chip select selection */\n#define XSPI_CR_FTHRES_Pos      16\n#define XSPI_CR_FTHRES_Msk      (0x1f << 16) /* FIFO threshold */\n#define XSPI_CR_TEIE_Pos        20\n#define XSPI_CR_TEIE            (1 << 20)  /* Transfer error interrupt enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_TCIE_Pos        21\n#define XSPI_CR_TCIE            (1 << 21)  /* Transfer complete interrupt enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_FTIE_Pos        22\n#define XSPI_CR_FTIE            (1 << 22)  /* FIFO threshold interrupt enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_SMIE_Pos        23\n#define XSPI_CR_SMIE            (1 << 23)  /* Status match interrupt enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_TOIE_Pos        24\n#define XSPI_CR_TOIE            (1 << 24)  /* Timeout interrupt enable */\n#define XSPI_CR_APMS_Pos        26\n#define XSPI_CR_APMS            (1 << 26)  /* Automatic-polling mode stop */\n#define XSPI_CR_PMM_Pos         27\n#define XSPI_CR_PMM             (1 << 27)  /* Polling mode match */\n#define XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos       28\n#define XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk       (3 << 28)  /* Functional mode */\n#define XSPI_MSEL_Pos           4\n#define XSPI_MSEL_Msk           (3 << 4)   /* Memory selection */\n\n/* Functional mode values */\n#define XSPI_FMODE_INDIRECT_WR  0  /* Indirect write mode */\n#define XSPI_FMODE_INDIRECT_RD  1  /* Indirect read mode */\n#define XSPI_FMODE_AUTO_POLL    2  /* Automatic polling mode */\n#define XSPI_FMODE_MEMORY_MAPPED 3 /* Memory-mapped mode */\n\n/* XSPI Device Configuration Register 1 (DCR1) ******************************/\n\n#define XSPI_DCR1_CKMODE_Pos    0\n#define XSPI_DCR1_CKMODE        (1 << 0)   /* Clock mode */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_FRCK_Pos      1\n#define XSPI_DCR1_FRCK          (1 << 1)   /* Free-running clock */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_CSHT_Pos      8\n#define XSPI_DCR1_CSHT_Msk      (0x3f << 8)  /* Chip select high time */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_DEVSIZE_Pos   16\n#define XSPI_DCR1_DEVSIZE_Msk   (0x1f << 16) /* Device size */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_Pos      24\n#define XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_Msk      (7 << 24)  /* Memory type */\n\n/* Memory type values */\n#define XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_MICRON   0\n#define XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_MACRONIX 1\n#define XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_ADESTO   2\n\n/* XSPI Device Configuration Register 2 (DCR2) ******************************/\n\n#define XSPI_DCR2_PRESCALER_Pos 0\n#define XSPI_DCR2_PRESCALER_Msk (0xff << 0)  /* Clock prescaler */\n#define XSPI_DCR2_WRAPSIZE_Pos  16\n#define XSPI_DCR2_WRAPSIZE_Msk  (3 << 16)   /* Wrap size */\n\n/* XSPI Status Register (SR) ************************************************/\n\n#define XSPI_SR_TEF_Pos         0\n#define XSPI_SR_TEF             (1 << 0)   /* Transfer error flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_TCF_Pos         1\n#define XSPI_SR_TCF             (1 << 1)   /* Transfer complete flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_FTF_Pos         2\n#define XSPI_SR_FTF             (1 << 2)   /* FIFO threshold flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_SMF_Pos         3\n#define XSPI_SR_SMF             (1 << 3)   /* Status match flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_TOF_Pos         4\n#define XSPI_SR_TOF             (1 << 4)   /* Timeout flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_BUSY_Pos        5\n#define XSPI_SR_BUSY            (1 << 5)   /* Busy flag */\n#define XSPI_SR_FLEVEL_Pos      8\n#define XSPI_SR_FLEVEL_Msk      (0x3f << 8) /* FIFO level */\n\n/* XSPI Flag Clear Register (FCR) *******************************************/\n\n#define XSPI_FCR_CTEF           (1 << 0)   /* Clear transfer error flag */\n#define XSPI_FCR_CTCF           (1 << 1)   /* Clear transfer complete flag */\n#define XSPI_FCR_CSMF           (1 << 3)   /* Clear status match flag */\n#define XSPI_FCR_CTOF           (1 << 4)   /* Clear timeout flag */\n\n/* XSPI Communication Configuration Register (CCR) **************************/\n\n#define XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos      0\n#define XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Msk      (7 << 0)   /* Instruction mode */\n#define XSPI_CCR_IDTR_Pos       3\n#define XSPI_CCR_IDTR           (1 << 3)   /* Instruction DTR */\n#define XSPI_CCR_ISIZE_Pos      4\n#define XSPI_CCR_ISIZE          (1 << 4)   /* Instruction size (0=8bit, 1=16bit) */\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos     8\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Msk     (7 << 8)   /* Address mode */\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADDTR_Pos      11\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADDTR          (1 << 11)  /* Address DTR */\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos     12\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Msk     (3 << 12)  /* Address size */\n#define XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos      16\n#define XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Msk      (7 << 16)  /* Data mode */\n#define XSPI_CCR_DDTR_Pos       19\n#define XSPI_CCR_DDTR           (1 << 19)  /* Data DTR */\n#define XSPI_CCR_DQSE_Pos       20\n#define XSPI_CCR_DQSE           (1 << 20)  /* DQS enable */\n\n/* Line mode values */\n#define XSPI_CCR_MODE_NONE      0  /* No data/instruction/address */\n#define XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE     1  /* 1 line */\n#define XSPI_CCR_MODE_2LINES    2  /* 2 lines */\n#define XSPI_CCR_MODE_4LINES    3  /* 4 lines */\n#define XSPI_CCR_MODE_8LINES    4  /* 8 lines */\n\n/* Address size values */\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_8BIT    0\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_16BIT   1\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_24BIT   2\n#define XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_32BIT   3\n\n/* XSPI Timing Configuration Register (TCR) *********************************/\n\n#define XSPI_TCR_DCYC_Pos       0\n#define XSPI_TCR_DCYC_Msk       (0x1f << 0)  /* Number of dummy cycles */\n\n/* XSPIM (IO Manager) registers *********************************************/\n\n#define XSPIM_CR_OFFSET         0x0000  /* XSPIM control register */\n\n/* RCC AHB5 enable/reset bits ***********************************************/\n\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPIMEN_Pos 0\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPIMEN     (1 << 0)  /* XSPIM clock enable */\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI1EN_Pos 1\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI1EN     (1 << 1)  /* XSPI1 clock enable */\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI2EN_Pos 2\n#define RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI2EN     (1 << 2)  /* XSPI2 clock enable */\n\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST_Pos 0\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST   (1 << 0)  /* XSPIM reset */\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST_Pos 1\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST   (1 << 1)  /* XSPI1 reset */\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST_Pos 2\n#define RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST   (1 << 2)  /* XSPI2 reset */\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Inline Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* XSPI register access macros **********************************************/\n\n#define XSPI1_BASE  STM32_XSPI1_BASE\n#define XSPI2_BASE  STM32_XSPI2_BASE\n#define XSPIM_BASE  STM32_XSPIM_BASE\n\n/* XSPI register structure (direct register access) */\n\ntypedef struct\n{\n  volatile uint32_t cr;       /* 0x00: Control register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res0;    /* 0x04: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t dcr1;     /* 0x08: Device configuration register 1 */\n  volatile uint32_t dcr2;     /* 0x0C: Device configuration register 2 */\n  volatile uint32_t dcr3;     /* 0x10: Device configuration register 3 */\n  volatile uint32_t dcr4;     /* 0x14: Device configuration register 4 */\n  volatile uint32_t _res1[2]; /* 0x18-0x1C: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t sr;       /* 0x20: Status register */\n  volatile uint32_t fcr;      /* 0x24: Flag clear register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res2[6]; /* 0x28-0x3C: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t dlr;      /* 0x40: Data length register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res3[47];/* 0x44-0xFC: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t ccr;      /* 0x100: Communication configuration register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res4;    /* 0x104: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t tcr;      /* 0x108: Timing configuration register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res5;    /* 0x10C: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t ir;       /* 0x110: Instruction register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res6;    /* 0x114: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t abr;      /* 0x118: Alternate bytes register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res7;    /* 0x11C: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t ar;       /* 0x120: Address register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res8[2]; /* 0x124-0x128: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t dr;       /* 0x130: Data register */\n  volatile uint32_t _res9;    /* 0x134: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t _res10[3];/* 0x138-0x140: Reserved */\n  volatile uint32_t lptr;     /* 0x144: Low-power timeout register */\n} xspi_regs_t;\n\n#define XSPI1_REGS  ((xspi_regs_t *)XSPI1_BASE)\n#define XSPI2_REGS  ((xspi_regs_t *)XSPI2_BASE)\n\n/* XSPIM register structure */\n\ntypedef struct\n{\n  volatile uint32_t cr;       /* 0x00: Control register */\n} xspim_regs_t;\n\n#define XSPIM_REGS  ((xspim_regs_t *)XSPIM_BASE)\n\n#endif /* __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_XSPI_H */\n","numLines":253,"startLine":1,"totalLines":253}},"displayPath":"arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"35ee2f99-b7ee-4e5e-ad26-3bc2104152d7","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.652Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"35ee2f99-b7ee-4e5e-ad26-3bc2104152d7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c","content":"/****************************************************************************\n * vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_224_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\n * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\n * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.\n * The ASF licenses this file to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n * (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with\n * the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\n *\n *   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n *\n * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n * WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n * See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n * limitations under the License.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader) for NUCLEO-N657X0-Q.\n *\n * This runs from SRAM2 after the hardware boot ROM loads it from\n * external flash offset 0.  Its job:\n *   1. Configure VDDIO3 (1.8V) for XSPI pins\n *   2. Initialize XSPI2 and switch flash to Octal DTR mode\n *   3. Enable memory-mapped mode (XIP)\n *   4. Jump to the main NuttX application at 0x70080000\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"arm_m_nvic.h\"\n#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h\"\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Application entry point in external flash */\n\n#define APP_ENTRY_ADDR    0x70080000\n\n/* BSEC OTP fuse for VDDIO3 high-speed IO optimization */\n\n#define BSEC_HW_CONFIG_ID     124\n#define BSEC_HWS_HSLV_VDDIO3  (1 << 15)\n\n/* PWR register addresses (simplified for FSBL) */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR_OFFSET   0x00   /* AHB4 enable register offset */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB4ENR2_OFFSET  0x04   /* APB4 enable register 2 offset */\n\n/* RCC AHB4/APB4 enable bits */\n\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_PWREN_Pos      31\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_PWREN          (1 << 31)\n\n#define RCC_APB4HEN2_BSECEN_Pos    0\n#define RCC_APB4HEN2_BSECEN        (1 << 0)\n#define RCC_APB4HEN2_SYSCFGEN_Pos  1\n#define RCC_APB4HEN2_SYSCFGEN      (1 << 1)\n\n/* PWR registers for VDDIO3 configuration */\n\n#define PWR_BASE            0x46020800UL\n#define PWR_OFFSET_VDDIO3CR  0x34  /* VDDIO3 control register offset */\n\n/* SYSCFG registers for IO compensation */\n\n#define SYSCFG_BASE         0x46020400UL\n#define SYSCFG_VDDIO3CCCR_OFFSET  0x28\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Configure VDDIO domains for XSPI flash pins */\n\nstatic void fsbl_config_vdd(void)\n{\n  /* Enable PWR, BSEC, SYSCFG clocks */\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR, 0, RCC_AHB4ENR_PWREN);\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_APB4HENR, 0, RCC_APB4HEN2_BSECEN |\n                                      RCC_APB4HEN2_SYSCFGEN);\n\n  /* Configure VDDIO3 for 1.8V (XSPI pins PN0-PN11 are on VDDIO3)\n   *\n   * NOTE: The exact register layout depends on the STM32N6 variant.\n   * This is a simplified version.  For production code, use the\n   * STM32 HAL PWR functions.\n   */\n\n  /* Program OTP fuse for VDDIO3 high-speed mode if not already set.\n   *\n   * WARNING: This is a ONE-TIME irreversible operation (burns OTP fuse).\n   * Only do this once on a new board.  After that, the fuse persists.\n   *\n   * For initial development, we skip the fuse programming and just\n   * configure VDDIO3 for 1.8V without the HSLV optimization.\n   */\n\n  /* Enable VDDIO3 domain and set 1.8V range */\n\n  volatile uint32_t *pwr_vddio3cr =\n    (volatile uint32_t *)(PWR_BASE + PWR_OFFSET_VDDIO3CR);\n\n  /* Set VDDIO3 voltage range to 1.8V (bit 0 = 0 for 1.8V, 1 for 3.3V) */\n\n  *pwr_vddio3cr &= ~(1 << 0);  /* 1.8V range */\n\n  /* Enable IO compensation for VDDIO3 */\n\n  volatile uint32_t *syscfg_vddio3cccr =\n    (volatile uint32_t *)(SYSCFG_BASE + SYSCFG_VDDIO3CCCR_OFFSET);\n\n  *syscfg_vddio3cccr |= (1 << 0);  /* Enable compensation cell */\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: fsbl_entry\n *\n * Description:\n *   Entry point for the FSBL.  Called by the hardware boot ROM after\n *   loading this code from flash offset 0 into SRAM2 at 0x34180400.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid fsbl_entry(void)\n{\n  /* Set vector table to our location */\n\n  SCB->VTOR = 0x34180400;\n\n  /* Configure power domains for XSPI */\n\n  fsbl_config_vdd();\n\n  /* Initialize XSPI2 and enable memory-mapped flash */\n\n  stm32n6_xspi_initialize();\n\n  /* Jump to main application in external flash (XIP) */\n\n  /* The application's vector table is at 0x70080000:\n   *   [0] = Initial stack pointer\n   *   [1] = Reset handler address\n   */\n\n  uint32_t app_sp  = *(volatile uint32_t *)(APP_ENTRY_ADDR);\n  uint32_t app_pc  = *(volatile uint32_t *)(APP_ENTRY_ADDR + 4);\n\n  /* Set stack pointer */\n\n  __asm__ volatile (\"msr msp, %0\" :: \"r\" (app_sp));\n\n  /* Jump to application */\n\n  void (*app_reset)(void) = (void (*)(void))app_pc;\n  app_reset();\n\n  /* Should never reach here */\n\n  for (;;);\n}\n","numLines":183,"startLine":1,"totalLines":183}},"displayPath":"../contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_fsbl.c"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b74ede0-9eb7-49aa-9c73-c82f8ff946a3","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.713Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"9b74ede0-9eb7-49aa-9c73-c82f8ff946a3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h","content":"/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\n * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\n * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.  The\n * ASF licenses this file to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the\n * \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the\n * License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\n *\n *   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n *\n * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT\n * WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.  See the\n * License for the specific language governing permissions and limitations\n * under the License.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#ifndef __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_RCC_H\n#define __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_RCC_H\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h\"\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Register Offsets *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CR_OFFSET           0x0000  /* Clock control register */\n#define STM32_RCC_SR_OFFSET           0x0004  /* Clock status register */\n#define STM32_RCC_CFGR1_OFFSET        0x0020  /* Clock configuration register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_CFGR2_OFFSET        0x0024  /* Clock configuration register 2 */\n#define STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR1_OFFSET    0x0080  /* PLL1 configuration register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR3_OFFSET    0x0088  /* PLL1 configuration register 3 */\n#define STM32_RCC_IC1CFGR_OFFSET      0x00c4  /* IC1 configuration register */\n#define STM32_RCC_IC2CFGR_OFFSET      0x00c8  /* IC2 configuration register */\n#define STM32_RCC_IC3CFGR_OFFSET      0x00cc  /* IC3 configuration register */\n#define STM32_RCC_IC6CFGR_OFFSET      0x00d8  /* IC6 configuration register */\n#define STM32_RCC_IC11CFGR_OFFSET     0x00ec  /* IC11 configuration register */\n#define STM32_RCC_CCIPR13_OFFSET      0x0174  /* Peripheral kernel clock select register 13 */\n\n/* Peripheral clock enable / set / clear register offsets.  Each enable\n * register (xxxENR) has a paired set register (xxxENSR) that performs an\n * atomic OR and a clear register (xxxENCR) that performs an atomic AND\n * (Reference: RM0486 14.5).  The same triplet pattern applies to the LPENR\n * (sleep mode) registers.\n */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMENR_OFFSET       0x024c  /* AXI/AHB SRAM clock enable register */\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR_OFFSET      0x025c  /* AHB4 peripheral clock enable register */\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR_OFFSET      0x0260  /* AHB5 peripheral clock enable register */\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR_OFFSET     0x0264  /* AHB5 peripheral reset register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LENR_OFFSET     0x0264  /* APB1 peripheral clock enable register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENR_OFFSET      0x026c  /* APB2 peripheral clock enable register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB4HENR_OFFSET     0x0278  /* APB4 peripheral clock enable register 2 */\n#define STM32_RCC_BUSLPENR_OFFSET     0x0284  /* Bus clocks enable in Sleep mode */\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMLPENR_OFFSET     0x028c  /* SRAM clocks enable in Sleep mode */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENR_OFFSET   0x02a4  /* APB1 LP clock enable register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2LPENR_OFFSET    0x02ac  /* APB2 LP clock enable register */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_DIVENR_OFFSET       0x0240  /* IC divider enable register */\n#define STM32_RCC_DIVENSR_OFFSET      0x0a40  /* IC divider enable set register */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMENSR_OFFSET      0x0a4c  /* SRAM clock enable set register */\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB4ENSR_OFFSET     0x0a5c  /* AHB4 clock enable set register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LENSR_OFFSET    0x0a64  /* APB1 clock enable set register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENSR_OFFSET     0x0a6c  /* APB2 clock enable set register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB4HENSR_OFFSET    0x0a78  /* APB4 clock enable set register 2 */\n#define STM32_RCC_BUSLPENSR_OFFSET    0x0a84  /* Bus LP clock enable set register */\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMLPENSR_OFFSET    0x0a8c  /* SRAM LP clock enable set register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENSR_OFFSET  0x0aa4  /* APB1 LP clock enable set register 1 */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2LPENSR_OFFSET   0x0aac  /* APB2 LP clock enable set register */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CCR_OFFSET          0x1000  /* Clock control clear register */\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENCR_OFFSET     0x126c  /* APB2 clock enable clear register */\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CSR_OFFSET          0x0800  /* Clock status (set) register */\n\n/* Register Addresses *******************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CR                  (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_SR                  (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_SR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_CFGR1               (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CFGR1_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_CFGR2               (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CFGR2_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR1           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR1_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR3           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_PLL1CFGR3_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_IC1CFGR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_IC1CFGR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_IC2CFGR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_IC2CFGR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_IC3CFGR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_IC3CFGR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_IC6CFGR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_IC6CFGR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_IC11CFGR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_IC11CFGR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_CCIPR13             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CCIPR13_OFFSET)\n\n#define STM32_RCC_DIVENR              (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_DIVENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_DIVENSR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_DIVENSR_OFFSET)\n\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMENR              (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_MEMENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LENR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB1LENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB2ENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB4HENR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB4HENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_BUSLPENR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_BUSLPENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMLPENR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_MEMLPENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENR          (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2LPENR           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB2LPENR_OFFSET)\n\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMENSR             (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_MEMENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_AHB4ENSR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_AHB4ENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LENSR           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB1LENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENSR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB2ENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB4HENSR           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB4HENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_BUSLPENSR           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_BUSLPENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_MEMLPENSR           (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_MEMLPENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENSR         (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB1LLPENSR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2LPENSR          (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB2LPENSR_OFFSET)\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CCR                 (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CCR_OFFSET)\n#define STM32_RCC_APB2ENCR            (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_APB2ENCR_OFFSET)\n\n#define STM32_RCC_CSR                 (STM32_RCC_BASE + STM32_RCC_CSR_OFFSET)\n\n/* Register Bitfield Definitions ********************************************/\n\n/* Clock control register */\n\n#define RCC_CR_PLL1ON                 (1 << 8)  /* Bit 8:  PLL1 enable */\n#define RCC_CR_HSION                  (1 << 3)  /* Bit 3:  HSI enable */\n\n/* Clock status register */\n\n#define RCC_SR_PLL1RDY                (1 << 8)  /* Bit 8:  PLL1 clock ready */\n#define RCC_SR_HSIRDY                 (1 << 3)  /* Bit 3:  HSI clock ready */\n\n/* Clock configuration register 1.  SYSSW = 0b11 selects three IC dividers\n * (IC2 for SYSCLK, IC6 for AHB, IC11 for APB) -- the SVD names this state\n * after the first IC only.\n */\n\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSWS_SHIFT        (28)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSWS_MASK         (0x3 << RCC_CFGR1_SYSSWS_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSWS_IC2_IC6_IC11 (3 << RCC_CFGR1_SYSSWS_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSW_SHIFT         (24)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSW_MASK          (0x3 << RCC_CFGR1_SYSSW_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_SYSSW_IC2_IC6_IC11  (3 << RCC_CFGR1_SYSSW_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSWS_SHIFT        (20)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSWS_MASK         (0x3 << RCC_CFGR1_CPUSWS_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSWS_IC1          (3 << RCC_CFGR1_CPUSWS_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSW_SHIFT         (16)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSW_MASK          (0x3 << RCC_CFGR1_CPUSW_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR1_CPUSW_IC1           (3 << RCC_CFGR1_CPUSW_SHIFT)\n\n/* Clock configuration register 2.  HPRE divides the SYSCLK fed to AHB\n * before it reaches the CPU/peripheral bus matrix.\n */\n\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT          (20)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_MASK           (0x7 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SYSCLK         (0 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SYSCLKd2       (1 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SYSCLKd4       (2 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SYSCLKd8       (3 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SYSCLKd16      (4 << RCC_CFGR2_HPRE_SHIFT)\n\n#define RCC_CFGR2                     STM32_RCC_CFGR2\n\n/* PLL1 configuration register 1 */\n\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_SEL_SHIFT       (28)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_SEL_MASK        (0x7 << RCC_PLL1CFGR1_SEL_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_SEL_HSI         (0 << RCC_PLL1CFGR1_SEL_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVM_SHIFT      (20)       /* Bits 25-20: Reference divider */\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVM_MASK       (0x3f << RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVM_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVN_SHIFT      (8)        /* Bits 19-8: Feedback divider */\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVN_MASK       (0xfff << RCC_PLL1CFGR1_DIVN_SHIFT)\n\n/* PLL1 configuration register 3 */\n\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIVEN          (1 << 30)  /* Bit 30: Post-divider and PLL output enable */\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV1_SHIFT     (27)       /* Bits 29-27: Post-divider 1 */\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV1_MASK      (0x7 << RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV1_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV2_SHIFT     (24)       /* Bits 26-24: Post-divider 2 */\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV2_MASK      (0x7 << RCC_PLL1CFGR3_PDIV2_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_PLL1CFGR3_MODSSDIS        (1 << 2)   /* Bit 2:  Modulation spread spectrum disable */\n\n/* IC1..IC20 configuration registers -- all share the same layout.  Field\n * SEL selects the PLL source (PLL1..PLL4); field INT is an 8-bit integer\n * divider where INT[7:0] = N-1 yielding a divide ratio of N.\n */\n\n#define RCC_ICCFGR_SEL_SHIFT          (28)\n#define RCC_ICCFGR_SEL_MASK           (0x3 << RCC_ICCFGR_SEL_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_ICCFGR_SEL_PLL1           (0 << RCC_ICCFGR_SEL_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_ICCFGR_INT_SHIFT          (16)\n#define RCC_ICCFGR_INT_MASK           (0xff << RCC_ICCFGR_INT_SHIFT)\n\n/* IC divider enable register */\n\n#define RCC_DIVENR_IC11EN             (1 << 10)  /* Bit 10: IC11 enable */\n#define RCC_DIVENR_IC6EN              (1 << 5)   /* Bit 5:  IC6 enable */\n#define RCC_DIVENR_IC3EN              (1 << 2)   /* Bit 2:  IC3 enable */\n#define RCC_DIVENR_IC2EN              (1 << 1)   /* Bit 1:  IC2 enable */\n#define RCC_DIVENR_IC1EN              (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  IC1 enable */\n\n/* SRAM clock enable register */\n\n#define RCC_MEMENR_CACHEAXIRAMEN      (1 << 10)  /* Bit 10: CACHEAXIRAM enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM2EN         (1 << 8)   /* Bit 8:  AXISRAM2 enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM1EN         (1 << 7)   /* Bit 7:  AXISRAM1 enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM6EN         (1 << 3)   /* Bit 3:  AXISRAM6 enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM5EN         (1 << 2)   /* Bit 2:  AXISRAM5 enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM4EN         (1 << 1)   /* Bit 1:  AXISRAM4 enable */\n#define RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM3EN         (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  AXISRAM3 enable */\n\n#define RCC_MEMENR_ALLAXISRAM         (RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM1EN | RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM2EN | \\\n                                       RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM3EN | RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM4EN | \\\n                                       RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM5EN | RCC_MEMENR_AXISRAM6EN)\n\n/* AHB4 peripheral clock enable register */\n\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_PWREN             (1 << 18)  /* Bit 18: PWR enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOQEN           (1 << 16)  /* Bit 16: GPIOQ enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOPEN           (1 << 15)  /* Bit 15: GPIOP enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOOEN           (1 << 14)  /* Bit 14: GPIOO enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIONEN           (1 << 13)  /* Bit 13: GPION enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOHEN           (1 << 7)   /* Bit 7:  GPIOH enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOGEN           (1 << 6)   /* Bit 6:  GPIOG enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOFEN           (1 << 5)   /* Bit 5:  GPIOF enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOEEN           (1 << 4)   /* Bit 4:  GPIOE enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIODEN           (1 << 3)   /* Bit 3:  GPIOD enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOCEN           (1 << 2)   /* Bit 2:  GPIOC enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOBEN           (1 << 1)   /* Bit 1:  GPIOB enable */\n#define RCC_AHB4ENR_GPIOAEN           (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  GPIOA enable */\n\n/* APB1 peripheral clock enable register 1 */\n\n#define RCC_APB1LENR_TIM2EN           (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  TIM2 enable */\n\n/* APB2 peripheral clock enable register */\n\n#define RCC_APB2ENR_USART1EN          (1 << 4)   /* Bit 4:  USART1 enable */\n\n/* APB4 peripheral clock enable register 2 */\n\n#define RCC_APB4HENR_BSECEN           (1 << 1)   /* Bit 1:  BSEC enable */\n#define RCC_APB4HENR_SYSCFGEN         (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  SYSCFG enable */\n\n/* Bus clock enable in Sleep mode */\n\n#define RCC_BUSLPENR_ACLKNCLPEN       (1 << 1)   /* Bit 1:  ACLKNC clock enable in CSLEEP */\n#define RCC_BUSLPENR_ACLKNLPEN        (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  ACLKN clock enable in CSLEEP */\n\n/* SRAM clock enable in Sleep mode */\n\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_CACHEAXIRAMLPEN  (1 << 10)  /* Bit 10: CACHEAXIRAM enable in CSLEEP */\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM2LPEN     (1 << 8)\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM1LPEN     (1 << 7)\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM6LPEN     (1 << 3)\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM5LPEN     (1 << 2)\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM4LPEN     (1 << 1)\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM3LPEN     (1 << 0)\n\n#define RCC_MEMLPENR_ALLAXISRAM       (RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM1LPEN | RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM2LPEN | \\\n                                       RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM3LPEN | RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM4LPEN | \\\n                                       RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM5LPEN | RCC_MEMLPENR_AXISRAM6LPEN)\n\n/* APB1 peripheral clock enable in Sleep mode (register 1) */\n\n#define RCC_APB1LLPENR_TIM2LPEN       (1 << 0)   /* Bit 0:  TIM2 enable in CSLEEP */\n\n/* APB2 peripheral clock enable in Sleep mode */\n\n#define RCC_APB2LPENR_USART1LPEN      (1 << 4)   /* Bit 4:  USART1 enable in CSLEEP */\n\n/* Peripheral kernel clock select register 13 */\n\n#define RCC_CCIPR13_USART1SEL_SHIFT   (0)\n#define RCC_CCIPR13_USART1SEL_MASK    (0x7 << RCC_CCIPR13_USART1SEL_SHIFT)\n#define RCC_CCIPR13_USART1SEL_HSI     (6 << RCC_CCIPR13_USART1SEL_SHIFT)\n\n#endif /* __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_RCC_H */\n","numLines":293,"startLine":1,"totalLines":293}},"displayPath":"arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d150aecb-69ce-4273-9b3e-c74f8348192d","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.727Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"d150aecb-69ce-4273-9b3e-c74f8348192d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h","content":"/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\n * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\n * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.  The\n * ASF licenses this file to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the\n * \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with the\n * License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\n *\n *   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n *\n * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT\n * WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.  See the\n * License for the specific language governing permissions and limitations\n * under the License.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#ifndef __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_MEMORYMAP_H\n#define __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_MEMORYMAP_H\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* STM32N6XXX Address Blocks ************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_CODE_BASE       0x00000000    /* 0x00000000-0x1fffffff: 512Mb code block */\n#define STM32_SRAM_BASE       0x34000000    /* 0x34000000: SRAM (no internal flash) */\n#define STM32_PERIPH_BASE     0x40000000    /* 0x40000000-0x5fffffff: 512Mb peripheral block */\n#define STM32_CORTEX_BASE     0xe0000000    /* 0xe0000000-0xffffffff: 512Mb Cortex-M55 block */\n\n#define STM32_REGION_MASK     0xf0000000\n#define STM32_IS_SRAM(a)      ((((uint32_t)(a)) & STM32_REGION_MASK) == 0x30000000)\n\n/* SRAM Addresses ***********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_SRAM1_BASE      0x34000000    /* SRAM1 base */\n#define STM32_SRAM2_BASE      0x34100000    /* SRAM2 base */\n\n/* External Memory **********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_XSPI1_BANK      0x90000000    /* XSPI1 memory-mapped region */\n#define STM32_XSPI2_BANK      0x70000000    /* XSPI2 memory-mapped region */\n\n/* Peripheral Base Addresses ************************************************\n *\n * Each peripheral is physically aliased twice: a Non-Secure alias at\n * 0x4xxxxxxx and a Secure alias at 0x5xxxxxxx (RM0486 section 3.5.1).\n * The same hardware register is reached through either alias.\n *\n * In DEV boot mode the CPU runs in Secure state with SAU disabled and\n * SAU_CTRL.ALLNS=0, so the SAU unilaterally marks every address as\n * Secure regardless of which alias is used; both aliases therefore work\n * for register access from this port.\n *\n * We pick the Secure aliases consistently to match the register listings\n * in the Reference Manual and to leave the Non-Secure aliases free for a\n * future Non-Secure world.\n *\n * Secure alias = Non-Secure alias + 0x10000000\n */\n\n#define STM32_APB1_BASE       0x50000000    /* APB1 (Secure) */\n#define STM32_APB2_BASE       0x52000000    /* APB2 (Secure) */\n#define STM32_APB4_BASE       0x56000000    /* APB4 (Secure) */\n#define STM32_APB5_BASE       0x58000000    /* APB5 (Secure) - LTDC/DCMIPP/CSI2/GFXTIM/VENC */\n#define STM32_AHB4_BASE       0x56020000    /* AHB4 (Secure) */\n\n/* APB1 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_TIM2_BASE       0x50000000\n#define STM32_TIM3_BASE       0x50000400\n#define STM32_TIM4_BASE       0x50000800\n#define STM32_TIM5_BASE       0x50000c00\n#define STM32_TIM6_BASE       0x50001000\n#define STM32_TIM7_BASE       0x50001400\n#define STM32_LPTIM1_BASE     0x50002400\n#define STM32_SPI2_BASE       0x50003800\n#define STM32_SPI3_BASE       0x50003c00\n#define STM32_USART2_BASE     0x50004400\n#define STM32_USART3_BASE     0x50004800\n#define STM32_UART4_BASE      0x50004c00\n#define STM32_UART5_BASE      0x50005000\n#define STM32_I2C1_BASE       0x50005400\n#define STM32_I2C2_BASE       0x50005800\n#define STM32_I2C3_BASE       0x50005c00\n\n/* APB2 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_TIM1_BASE       0x52000000\n#define STM32_TIM8_BASE       0x52000400\n#define STM32_USART1_BASE     0x52001000\n#define STM32_SPI1_BASE       0x52003000\n#define STM32_SPI4_BASE       0x52003400\n#define STM32_TIM15_BASE      0x52004000\n#define STM32_TIM16_BASE      0x52004400\n#define STM32_TIM17_BASE      0x52004800\n#define STM32_SPI5_BASE       0x52005000\n\n/* APB4 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_SPI6_BASE       0x56001400\n#define STM32_I2C4_BASE       0x56001c00\n#define STM32_LPTIM2_BASE     0x56002400\n#define STM32_LPTIM3_BASE     0x56002800\n#define STM32_LPTIM4_BASE     0x56002c00\n#define STM32_LPTIM5_BASE     0x56003000\n\n/* APB4 peripherals (RTC on APB4 + 0x4000) **********************************/\n\n#define STM32_RTC_BASE        0x56004000\n#define STM32_TAMP_BASE       0x56004400\n#define STM32_IWDG_BASE       0x56004800\n#define STM32_BSEC_BASE       0x56009000\n#define STM32_DTS_BASE        0x5600a000\n\n/* AHB4 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_GPIOA_BASE      0x56020000\n#define STM32_GPIOB_BASE      0x56020400\n#define STM32_GPIOC_BASE      0x56020800\n#define STM32_GPIOD_BASE      0x56020c00\n#define STM32_GPIOE_BASE      0x56021000\n#define STM32_GPIOF_BASE      0x56021400\n#define STM32_GPIOG_BASE      0x56021800\n#define STM32_GPIOH_BASE      0x56021c00\n#define STM32_GPION_BASE      0x56023400\n#define STM32_GPIOO_BASE      0x56023800\n#define STM32_GPIOP_BASE      0x56023c00\n#define STM32_GPIOQ_BASE      0x56024000\n\n#define STM32_CRC_BASE        0x56024c00\n#define STM32_PWR_BASE        0x56024800\n#define STM32_EXTI_BASE       0x56025000\n#define STM32_RCC_BASE        0x56028000\n\n/* AHB1 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_GPDMA1_BASE     0x50021000    /* GPDMA1 (AHB1, Secure) */\n#define STM32_ADC1_BASE       0x50022000    /* ADC1 (AHB1, Secure) */\n#define STM32_ADC2_BASE       0x50022100    /* ADC2 (AHB1, Secure) */\n#define STM32_ADC12_COMMON_BASE 0x50022300  /* ADC1/2 common (AHB1, Secure) */\n\n/* AHB3 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_RNG_BASE        0x54020000    /* RNG (AHB3, Secure) */\n#define STM32_RIFSC_BASE      0x54024000    /* RIFSC (AHB3, Secure) */\n\n/* AHB2 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_RAMCFG_BASE     0x52023000    /* RAMCFG (AHB2, Secure) */\n\n/* AHB5 peripherals *********************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_AHB5_BASE       0x58020000    /* AHB5 (Secure) */\n#define STM32_HPDMA1_BASE     0x58020000    /* HPDMA1 (AHB5, Secure) */\n#define STM32_XSPI1_BASE      0x58029000    /* XSPI1 controller (AHB5, Secure) */\n#define STM32_XSPI2_BASE      0x5802A000    /* XSPI2 controller (AHB5, Secure) */\n#define STM32_XSPIM_BASE      0x5802B400    /* XSPIM IO Manager (AHB5, Secure) */\n#define STM32_USB1_HS_PHYC_BASE 0x5803FC00  /* USB1 HS PHY controller (Secure) */\n#define STM32_USB1_OTG_HS_BASE  0x58040000  /* USB1 OTG HS (Secure) */\n#define STM32_USB2_OTG_HS_BASE  0x58080000  /* USB2 OTG HS (Secure) */\n#define STM32_USB2_HS_PHYC_BASE 0x580C0000  /* USB2 HS PHY controller (Secure) */\n\n/* SYSCFG *******************************************************************/\n\n#define STM32_SYSCFG_BASE     0x56008000    /* SYSCFG (Secure) */\n\n#endif /* __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_HARDWARE_STM32N6XXX_MEMORYMAP_H */\n","numLines":175,"startLine":1,"totalLines":175}},"displayPath":"arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5bd4b6bc-d00a-4e43-9328-84e2bf16f97e","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.716Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"5bd4b6bc-d00a-4e43-9328-84e2bf16f97e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c","content":"/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\n * contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\n * this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.\n * The ASF licenses this file to you under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n * (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with\n * the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\n *\n *   http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n *\n * Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\n * distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\n * WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\n * See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\n * limitations under the License.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * XSPI2 driver for STM32N6 — controls external Macronix MX25UM51245G\n * flash in SPI and Octal DTR (DOPI) modes with memory-mapped XIP.\n *\n * Reference: atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include <nuttx/arch.h>\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <debug.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"stm32_gpio.h\"\n#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h\"\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* XSPI2 alternate function = 9 */\n\n#define XSPI2_AF  9\n\n/* Clock prescaler: F_CLK = F_AHB / PRESCALER\n * With HCLK=50MHz, prescaler=4 gives 12.5MHz for init\n */\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER\n#  define CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER  4\n#endif\n\n/* CS high time: nCS stays high for (CSHT+1) cycles */\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES\n#  define CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES  2\n#endif\n\n/* Macronix commands for SPI mode */\n\n#define CMD_WREN              0x06    /* Write enable */\n#define CMD_RDSR              0x05    /* Read status register */\n#define CMD_WRSCUR            0x72    /* Write security register */\n#define CMD_READ4B            0x13    /* 4-byte address read */\n\n/* Macronix commands for Octal DTR mode (16-bit, byte + complement) */\n\n#define CMD_8DTRD             0xee11  /* Octal DTR read */\n#define CMD_8DTRWREN          0x06f9  /* Octal DTR write enable */\n#define CMD_8DTRRDSR          0x05fa  /* Octal DTR read status */\n\n/* VDDIO3 and BSEC definitions */\n\n#define BSEC_HW_CONFIG_ID     124\n#define BSEC_HWS_HSLV_VDDIO3  (1 << 15)\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Data\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nstatic bool g_xspi_dtr_enabled = false;\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Configure a GPIO pin as XSPI alternate function */\n\nstatic inline void xspi_pinconfig(uint32_t pinset)\n{\n  stm32_configgpio(pinset | GPIO_SPEED_100MHZ);\n}\n\n/* Read 1 line (SPI mode) */\n\nstatic int xspi_read_111(xspi_regs_t *xspi, uint8_t cmd,\n                          bool has_addr, uint32_t addr,\n                          size_t len, uint8_t *dest)\n{\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE : XSPI_CCR_MODE_NONE;\n\n  xspi->cr = (xspi->cr & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (XSPI_FMODE_INDIRECT_RD << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->ccr =\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos)  |\n    (XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_32BIT << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos) |\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->tcr = 0;                    /* 0 dummy cycles */\n  xspi->dlr = len - 1;\n  xspi->ir = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->ar = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while ((xspi->sr >> XSPI_SR_FLEVEL_Pos) == 0)\n        {\n          if (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *dest++ = *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->dr;\n    }\n\n  xspi->fcr = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Write 1 line (SPI mode) */\n\nstatic int xspi_write_111(xspi_regs_t *xspi, uint8_t cmd,\n                           bool has_addr, uint32_t addr,\n                           size_t len, const uint8_t *src)\n{\n  uint32_t dmode = (len == 0) ? XSPI_CCR_MODE_NONE : XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE;\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE : XSPI_CCR_MODE_NONE;\n\n  xspi->cr = (xspi->cr & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (XSPI_FMODE_INDIRECT_WR << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->ccr =\n    (dmode << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos)  |\n    (XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_32BIT << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos) |\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->tcr = 0;\n\n  if (len != 0)\n    {\n      xspi->dlr = len - 1;\n    }\n\n  xspi->ir = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->ar = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while (!(xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_FTF))\n        {\n          if (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->dr = *src++;\n    }\n\n  while (!(xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_TCF))\n    {\n      if (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n        {\n          return -EIO;\n        }\n    }\n\n  xspi->fcr = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  while (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_BUSY);\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Switch flash from SPI mode to Octal DTR (DOPI) mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_switch_to_dtr(xspi_regs_t *xspi)\n{\n  uint8_t buf[4];\n\n  /* WREN in SPI mode */\n\n  xspi_write_111(xspi, CMD_WREN, false, 0, 0, NULL);\n\n  /* Wait WEL=1 */\n\n  for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 100; i++)\n    {\n      xspi_read_111(xspi, CMD_RDSR, false, 0, 1, buf);\n      if (buf[0] & 0x02)\n        {\n          break;\n        }\n    }\n\n  /* Write security register to enable DOPI mode:\n   * Address 0x00000000, data = 0x02\n   */\n\n  buf[0] = 0x02;\n  xspi_write_111(xspi, CMD_WRSCUR, true, 0x00000000, 1, buf);\n\n  g_xspi_dtr_enabled = true;\n}\n\n/* Enable memory-mapped mode in Octal DTR mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_memory_map_888(xspi_regs_t *xspi)\n{\n  xspi->ccr =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DQSE_Pos)  |   /* DQS enabled */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DDTR_Pos)  |   /* data DTR */\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_8LINES << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |   /* 8 lines */\n    (XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_32BIT << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ADDTR_Pos) |   /* address DTR */\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_8LINES << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ISIZE_Pos) |   /* 16-bit instruction */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IDTR_Pos)  |   /* instruction DTR */\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_8LINES << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);    /* 8 lines */\n\n  xspi->tcr = 20 << XSPI_TCR_DCYC_Pos;  /* 20 dummy cycles */\n  xspi->ir  = CMD_8DTRD;\n  xspi->lptr = 1024;\n\n  xspi->cr = (xspi->cr & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (XSPI_FMODE_MEMORY_MAPPED << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n}\n\n/* Enable memory-mapped mode in SPI (1-line) mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_memory_map_111(xspi_regs_t *xspi)\n{\n  xspi->ccr =\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |\n    (XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_32BIT << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos) |\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (XSPI_CCR_MODE_1LINE << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->tcr = 0;\n  xspi->ir  = CMD_READ4B;\n  xspi->lptr = 1024;\n\n  xspi->cr = (xspi->cr & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (XSPI_FMODE_MEMORY_MAPPED << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_initialize\n *\n * Description:\n *   Initialize XSPI2, configure pins, reset flash, switch to Octal DTR,\n *   and enable memory-mapped mode for XIP.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nint stm32n6_xspi_initialize(void)\n{\n  xspi_regs_t *xspi = XSPI2_REGS;\n\n  spiinfo(\"XSPI2: Initializing external flash...\\n\");\n\n  /* ---- Step 1: Configure XSPI2 GPIO pins (PN0-PN11, AF9) ---- */\n\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN0  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* DQS */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN1  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* CS */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN2  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO0 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN3  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO1 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN4  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO2 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN5  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO3 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN6  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* SCK */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN8  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO4 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN9  | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO5 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN10 | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO6 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_PORTN | GPIO_PIN11 | GPIO_AF9 | GPIO_PUSHPULL);  /* IO7 */\n\n  /* ---- Step 2: Enable clocks and release reset ---- */\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR, 0, RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST |\n                                        RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST |\n                                        RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST);\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR, RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST |\n                                     RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST |\n                                     RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST, 0);\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR, 0, RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPIMEN |\n                                      RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI1EN  |\n                                      RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI2EN);\n\n  /* ---- Step 3: Configure XSPIM in direct mode ---- */\n\n  XSPI1_REGS->cr &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPI2_REGS->cr &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPIM_REGS->cr = 0;   /* direct mode */\n\n  /* ---- Step 4: Configure XSPI2 peripheral ---- */\n\n  xspi->cr =\n    (3 << XSPI_CR_FTHRES_Pos) |  /* 4 bytes FIFO threshold */\n    (0 << XSPI_MSEL_Pos)      |  /* FLASH 0 */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_CSSEL_Pos)  |  /* use NCS1 */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_DMM_Pos)    |  /* no dual-memory */\n    (1 << XSPI_CR_TCEN_Pos)   |  /* timeout enabled */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_EN_Pos);       /* disabled for now */\n\n  xspi->dcr1 =\n    (XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_MACRONIX << XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_Pos) |\n    ((STM32N6_XSPI_FLASH_SIZE_LOG2 - 3 - 1) << XSPI_DCR1_DEVSIZE_Pos) |\n    ((CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES - 1) << XSPI_DCR1_CSHT_Pos) |\n    (0 << XSPI_DCR1_FRCK_Pos)   |  /* CLK not free-running */\n    (0 << XSPI_DCR1_CKMODE_Pos);   /* CLK idles low */\n\n  xspi->dcr2 =\n    ((CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER - 1) << XSPI_DCR2_PRESCALER_Pos);\n  xspi->dcr3 = 0;\n  xspi->dcr4 = 0;  /* refresh disabled (NOR flash) */\n  xspi->tcr = 0;\n\n  /* Enable XSPI2 */\n\n  xspi->cr |= XSPI_CR_EN;\n\n  /* Re-configure XSPIM */\n\n  XSPI1_REGS->cr &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPI2_REGS->cr &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPIM_REGS->cr = 0;\n  xspi->cr |= XSPI_CR_EN;\n\n  /* ---- Step 5: Switch flash to Octal DTR (DOPI) mode ---- */\n\n  xspi_switch_to_dtr(xspi);\n\n  /* ---- Step 6: Enable memory-mapped mode for XIP ---- */\n\n  xspi_memory_map_888(xspi);\n\n  spiinfo(\"XSPI2: Flash accessible at 0x%08x (64MB, Octal DTR XIP)\\n\",\n          STM32N6_XSPI2_XIP_BASE);\n\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit(void)\n{\n  xspi_regs_t *xspi = XSPI2_REGS;\n\n  if (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_BUSY)\n    {\n      xspi->cr |= XSPI_CR_ABORT;\n      while (!(xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_TCF));\n      xspi->fcr = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n      while (xspi->sr & XSPI_SR_BUSY);\n    }\n\n  xspi->cr = (xspi->cr & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (XSPI_FMODE_INDIRECT_WR << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable(void)\n{\n  if (g_xspi_dtr_enabled)\n    {\n      xspi_memory_map_888(XSPI2_REGS);\n    }\n  else\n    {\n      xspi_memory_map_111(XSPI2_REGS);\n    }\n}\n","numLines":406,"startLine":1,"totalLines":406}},"displayPath":"arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9a50a3f2-56b3-494d-aee7-3e9bf1031f31","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.731Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"9a50a3f2-56b3-494d-aee7-3e9bf1031f31","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"agent_listing_delta","addedTypes":["claude","claude-code-guide","Explore","general-purpose","Plan","statusline-setup"],"addedLines":["- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)","- claude-code-guide: Use this agent when the user asks questions (\"Can Claude...\", \"Does Claude...\", \"How do I...\") about: (1) Claude Code (the CLI tool) - features, hooks, slash commands, MCP servers, settings, IDE integrations, keyboard shortcuts; (2) Claude Agent SDK - building custom agents; (3) Claude API (formerly Anthropic API) - Messages API for directly passing messages to Claude, Tool Runner (`client.beta.messages.tool_runner`) for running an agentic loop over your own tools, manual tool-use loops, Managed Agents for server-hosted agents with a managed sandbox, prompt caching, and general Anthropic SDK usage; (4) Claude Tag (Claude in Slack) - what it is, setting it up for a Slack workspace, `/install-slack-app`; (5) `claude plugin eval` (writing and running plugin eval suites, its JSON/report, sandbox, CI, early-access enablement) and the `/skill-doctor` report. **IMPORTANT:** Before spawning a new agent, check if there is already a running or recently completed claude-code-guide agent that you can continue via SendMessage. (Tools: Bash, Read, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: \"medium\" for moderate exploration, \"very thorough\" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)","- Plan: Software architect agent for designing implementation plans. Use this when you need to plan the implementation strategy for a task. Returns step-by-step plans, identifies critical files, and considers architectural trade-offs. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- statusline-setup: Use this agent to configure the user's Claude Code status line setting. (Tools: Read, Edit)"],"removedTypes":[],"isInitial":true,"showConcurrencyNote":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"57c4cd42-61a3-42f6-95f2-12ad72e00576","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:34:21.733Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela/nuttx","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
