 me suggest trying a different approach - maybe using the boot ROM's DFU mode or using a different reset sequence.\n\nActually, I just realized something - the external loader file is1.89MB which is quite large. This suggests it contains the XSPI initialization code. But it might need specific conditions to work.\n\nLet me suggest trying:\n1. Hold the board in reset while connecting\n2. Use a different reset mode\n3. Check if there are any boot configuration jumpers\n\nI'll provide some troubleshooting suggestions.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":3710,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":56704}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"870552f6-4f75-48b1-a373-8a0c1f91716b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T15:35:12.574Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"2d4ac909-674d-4c60-84e6-9f60f265e8c3","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
